2 CONT
2 CONT Marie Louise Gonzaga de Nevers (known in Poland as Ludwika Maria) was Queen consort to two Polish kings: Władysław IV, and Jan II Kazimierz. She was born 18 August 1611 in Paris (or Nevers) to Prince Charles Gonzaga and Catherine 
2 CONC de Guise, princess of the French province of Maine.
2 CONT
2 CONT Contents
2 CONT
2 CONT [hide]
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 1 Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 2 Ancestors
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 3 Gallery
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 4 References
2 CONT
2 CONT     * 5 See also
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit] Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT After having spent her childhood with her mother, she was to have married Gaston, Duke of Orléans, in 1627, but King Louis XIII opposed the marriage and subsequently imprisoned her in the Vincennes fortress and later in a convent.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first proposal that she marry the King of Poland, Władysław IV, was made in 1634, but Władysław eventually married Cecilia Renata of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1640 Marie Louise met Władysław's brother, Jan Kazimierz, and started her literary salon in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia Renata died in 1644, and on 5 November 1645 Ludwika Maria married Władysław IV per procura (Jan Kazimierz representing his brother). She actually had to change her name from Maria to Ludwika Maria in order for the marriage
2 CONC  to take place, as in Poland the name Maria was at that time considered reserved for only Mary, Mother of Jesus.
2 CONT
2 CONT The proper wedding of Ludwika Maria and Władysław IV took place in Warsaw on 10 March 1646. Two years later, on 20 May 1648, Ludwika Maria was widowed by the death of Władysław IV. Jan Kazimierz was eventually elected the next Kin
2 CONC g of Poland, and married her on 30 May 1649. She died in Warsaw on 10 May 1667 and was buried in Kraków at Wawel Cathedral. Jan Kazimierz abdicated the Polish throne a year later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwika Maria was an active and energetic woman, with ambitious economic and political plans. The Polish nobility were scandalized at the Queen's meddling into politics, nevertheless she played an instrumental role in repulsing th
2 CONC e Swedish forces during the Deluge.
2 CONT
2 CONT She also founded the first Polish newspaper, Merkuriusz Polski (The Polish Mercury, 1652), and the first Polish convent of the Order of the Visitation of Holy Mary (1654). She supported Tito Livio Burattini, an extremely versatile
2 CONC  person, interested in mathematics, physics, astronomy, geodesy, economics, one of the first scientists dealing with ancient Egypt who also designed "flying machines". He lived in Poland since the early 1650s.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT After having spent her childhood with her mother, she was to have married Gaston, Duke of Orléans, in 1627, but King Louis XIII opposed the marriage and subsequently imprisoned her in the Vincennes fortress and later in a convent.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first proposal that she marry the King of Poland, Władysław IV, was made in 1634, but Władysław eventually married Cecilia Renata of Austria.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1640 Marie Louise met Władysław's brother, Jan Kazimierz, and started her literary salon in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia Renata died in 1644, and on 5 November 1645 Ludwika Maria married Władysław IV per procura (Jan Kazimierz representing his brother). She actually had to change her name from Maria to Ludwika Maria in order for the marriage
2 CONC  to take place, as in Poland the name Maria was at that time considered reserved for only Mary, Mother of Jesus.
2 CONT
2 CONT The proper wedding of Ludwika Maria and Władysław IV took place in Warsaw on 10 March 1646. Two years later, on 20 May 1648, Ludwika Maria was widowed by the death of Władysław IV. Jan Kazimierz was eventually elected the next Kin
2 CONC g of Poland, and married her on 30 May 1649. She died in Warsaw on 10 May 1667 and was buried in Kraków at Wawel Cathedral. Jan Kazimierz abdicated the Polish throne a year later.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ludwika Maria was an active and energetic woman, with ambitious economic and political plans. The Polish nobility were scandalized at the Queen's meddling into politics, nevertheless she played an instrumental role in repulsing th
2 CONC e Swedish forces during the Deluge.
2 CONT
2 CONT She also founded the first Polish newspaper, Merkuriusz Polski (The Polish Mercury, 1652), and the first Polish convent of the Order of the Visitation of Holy Mary (1654). She supported Tito Livio Burattini, an extremely versatile
2 CONC  person, interested in mathematics, physics, astronomy, geodesy, economics, one of the first scientists dealing with ancient Egypt who also designed "flying machines". He lived in Poland since the early 1650s.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT vend la seigneurie de Saint-Valery en 1640 a Nicolas-Joachim Rouault.
