2 CONT From Darryl Lundy's Peerage page on Amelia Anne Sophia Stanley:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Amelia Anne Sophia Stanley [1]
2 CONT *F, #22147, 
2 CONT *d. 22 February 1702/3
2 CONT *Last Edited=6 Mar 2011
2 CONT *Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Amelia Anne Sophia Stanley was the daughter of James Stanley, 7th Earl of Derby and Charlotte de la Trémoille.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She married John Murray, 1st Marquess of Athole, son of John Murray, 1st Earl of Atholl and Jean Campbell, on 5 May 1659.[1] 
2 CONT
2 CONT She died on 22 February 1702/3.[1] She was buried at Dunkeld, Perthshire, Scotland.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage:
2 CONT *As a result of her marriage, Lady Amelia Anne Sophia Stanley was styled as Countess of Atholl on 5 May 1659. 
2 CONT *From 5 May 1659, her married name became Murray. 
2 CONT *As a result of her marriage, Lady Amelia Anne Sophia Stanley was styled as Marchioness of Atholl on 17 February 1676.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Lady Amelia Anne Sophia Stanley and John Murray, 1st Marquess of Athole
2 CONT *1. Lady Amelia Murray+[2] d. 6 May 1743
2 CONT *2. John Murray, 1st Duke of Atholl+[1] b. 24 Feb 1659/60, d. 14 Nov 1724
2 CONT *3. Charles Murray, 1st Earl of Dunmore+[2] b. 24 Feb 1661, d. 19 Apr 1710
2 CONT *4. James Murray of Dowally+[2] b. 8 May 1663, d. 28 Dec 1719
2 CONT *5. William Murray, 2nd Lord Nairne+ b. 10 Dec 1664, d. 3 Feb 1726
2 CONT *6. Sir Mungo Murray [3] b. 1668, d. 1700
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT *1. [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lord Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Exti
2 CONC nct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan Sutton Publishing, 2000), volume I, page 316. Hereinafter cited as The Complete Peerage.
2 CONT *2. [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 134. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetag
2 CONC e, 106th edition.
