1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philibert-Emmanuel_de_Froulay,_chevalier_de_Tess%C3%A9
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert-Emmanuel de Froulay, chevalier de Tessé (1651 – Cremona, August 20, 1701), was baron d'Ambrières and a French army commander, fighting in the Williamite War in Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert-Emmanuel de Froulay was the younger brother of René de Froulay, count of Tessé.
2 CONT
2 CONT He fought in the Franco-Dutch War on several fronts. In 1684, during the War of the Reunions, he served in Flanders. At the outbreak of the Nine Years' War he was sent to fight with his brother in Germany, where he took part in th
2 CONC e devastation of the Palatinate. At the end of 1689, he was moved to Flanders.
2 CONT
2 CONT Made a brigadier of the Dragoons on March 10, 1690, he was promoted to Lieutenant General on January 30, 1691, and sent to Ireland to support King James II in the Williamite War in Ireland.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was second in command of the Franco-Irish army at the Battle of Aughrim under the Marquis de St Ruth. When Saint-Ruth was killed during the battle, the chevalier de Tessé could not prevent the collapse of his army. He became co
2 CONC mmander of the French troops during the Siege of Limerick (1691), and signed the Treaty of Limerick for France.
2 CONT
2 CONT After his return in France he fought many more battles, but died as Maréchal de camp from dysentery near Cremona on August 20 1701.
