1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://genealogics.org/getperson.php?personID=I00010094&tree=LEO
2 CONT
2 CONT BIOGRAPHY Elisabeth Pauline was born in Paris on 20 October 1737, the daughter of Alexandre de Gand-Vilain, comte de Middelburg, and Elisabeth de La Rochefoucauld. On 11 January 1755 in Paris she married Louis Léon Félicité de Bra
2 CONC ncas, duc de Lauraguais, duc de Brancas, son of Louis II de Brancas, duc de Lauraguais, and Adélaide Geneviève d'O, marquise de Franconville. They had two daughters of whom Louise Antoinette would have progeny, marrying Louis Pier
2 CONC re, prince et 5.duc d'Arenberg. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth was the principal heiress of her uncle Louis de Gand de Merode de Montmorency, 2.prince d'Isenghien, marshal of France, her father's elder brother. From him she inherited the title of Princesse d'Isenghien and part of th
2 CONC e enormous estate of the childless Philibert de Châlons, prince d'Orange et de Melfi (1502-1530), assigned to Louis de Gand by King Louis XV after a legal process stretching over two centuries (1530-1730). The estate included the 
2 CONC ruin of the massive 13th century fortress of Arlay in the former county of Burgundy (Franche-Comté). Arlay had been acquired by Jean 'l'Antique' de Châlons, comte de Bourgogne, d'Auxonne et de Chalon, in 1237. The fortress on a hi
2 CONC ll was augmented by subsequent generations who greatly prospered from their salt mines at Salins. Following the death of Charles 'the Bold', duke of Burgundy, at the Battle of Nancy in 1477, his great rival King Louis XI annexed t
2 CONC he county of Burgundy and ordered the demolition of the fortresses and castles of its lords, including the fortress of Arlay in 1479. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Philibert de Châlons left the titles of Prince d'Orange and Baron d'Arlay to his nephew René de Châlons. René died without surviving legitimate progeny, leaving the titles to his first cousin Willem I 'the Silent', prince of Orang
2 CONC e, Graf von Nassau. Hence Willem's descendant Beatrix, queen of The Netherlands, carries the titles of Princesse d'Orange and Baronne d'Arlay, and she still bears the motto of Châlons-Arlay, 'je maintiendrai', in French. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The former convent of the religious Order of Minims _(Ordo Fratrum Minimorum),_ situated below the ruins of the fortress of Arlay, was purchased by Elisabeth about 1770, when she was living at her château de Nozeroy in the High Ju
2 CONC ra. She renovated and extended the building as principal residence, adding an eight hectares park over the next ten years that encompassed the old fortress. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Elisabeth was arrested, tried and executed on the guillotine in Paris on 16 February 1794. Her husband escaped from the Terror by great good fortune, and died in December 1822
