1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude-Victor_de_Broglie
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Charles-Louis-Victor,_prince_de_Broglie
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles-Louis-Victor, prince de Broglie, called Victor de Broglie (22 September 1756 – 27 June 1794) was a French soldier and politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Victor de Broglie in Paris, the eldest son of Victor-François, 2nd duc de Broglie, the prince de Broglie attained the rank of maréchal de camp in the army. He adopted radical opinions and served with the Marquis de La Fayette and 
2 CONC the Comte de Rochambeau in the American War of Independence,
2 CONT
2 CONT The Prince was a member of the Jacobin Club, and sat in the National Constituent Assembly after the French Revolution, constantly voting on the Liberal side. He served as chief of the staff to the First Republic's Army on the Rhin
2 CONC e, but, during the Reign of Terror, he was denounced, arrested, and guillotined in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Since the old duc de Broglie survived him, the prince de Broglie's eldest son, Victor, eventually became the third duc de Broglie. The prince's dying admonition to his little son was to remain faithful to the principles of the Rev
2 CONC olution, however unjust and ungrateful it seemed then to be.
