2 CONT '''Rt. Rev. Lord George Murray''' was born on 30 January 1761. He was the son of Sir John Murray, 3rd Duke of Atholl and Lady Charlotte Murray, Baroness Strange. He married Anne Charlotte Grant, daughter of Lt.-Gen. Francis Grant 
2 CONC and Catherine Sophia Cox, on 18 December 1780.2 He died in 1803.
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Bishop of St. David's. '''Children of Rt. Rev. Lord George Murray and Anne Charlotte Grant'''
2 CONT * John Murray d. 1803
2 CONT * Charles Murray d. Jan 1808
2 CONT * Caroline Leonora Murray+ d. 8 Jan 1819
2 CONT * Rt. Rev. George Murray+ b. 12 Jan 1784, d. 16 Feb 1860
2 CONT * Louisa Ann Murray+ b. 29 May 1790, d. 21 Feb 1871
2 CONT * Reverend Edward Murray+ b. 5 Nov 1798, d. 1 Jul 1852
2 CONT * Henry Murray b.  Feb 1800, d. 26 Nov 1830
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.cracroftspeerage.co.uk/online/
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rt Rev Lord George Murray''' DD, Archdeacon of Manchester 1787, Rector of Hurston, co. Kent, and Dean of Bocking, Bishop of St David's 1800-03 (b. 30 Jan 1761;  d. 3 Jun 1803), mar. 18 Dec 1780 Anne Charlotte Grant, Lady-in-Wai
2 CONC ting to Queen Charlotte, only dau. of Lt Gen Francis Grant MP (by his wife Catherine Sophia Cox, 1st dau. of John Cox, of Stanford-in-the-Vale, co. Berkshire, by his wife Katharine Sophia Herbert, 2nd illegit. dau. of John [Sheffi
2 CONC eld], 1st Duke of Buckingham & Normanby, by his mistress Frances Stewart), 4th son of Sir James Grant of Grant, 6th Bt., by his wife Anne Colquhoun, only child and hrss. of Sir Humphrey Colquhoun of Luss, 5th Bt.,
