2 CONT ===Citations===
2 CONT
2 CONT * [S8] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage and Baronetage, 106th edition, 2 volumes (Crans, Switzerland: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 1999), volume 1, page 137. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Peerage and Baronetage,
2 CONC  106th edition.
2 CONT * [S37] Charles Mosley, editor, Burke's Peerage, Baronetage & Knightage, 107th edition, 3 volumes (Wilmington, Delaware, U.S.A.: Burke's Peerage (Genealogical Books) Ltd, 2003), volume 1, page 180. Hereinafter cited as Burke's Pee
2 CONC rage and Baronetage, 107th edition.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lord Henry was the son of the 3rd duke of Atholl. He was a soldier and administrator. He was the Colonel in chief of the Manx Fencibles 1795-1802. He had a son William James Athol Strange with his older Jewish mistress when he was
2 CONC  18 in 1783. In 1786 he married Eliza Kent and had a family with her. He was the fourth Lieutenant Governor of the Isle of Man. 
