1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *[http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexander_Gordon,_4th_Duke_of_Gordon Wikipedia Entry]
2 CONT *[http://www.bbc.co.uk/arts/yourpaintings/paintings/alexander-gordon-4th-duke-of-gordon-205872 BBC - Your Paintings - Alexander Gordon, 4th Duke of Gordon]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Gordon, 4th Duke of Gordon KT (18 June 1743 – 17 June 1827), styled Marquess of Huntly until 1752, was a Scottish nobleman, described by Kaimes as the "greatest subject in Britain", and was also known as the Cock o' the 
2 CONC North, the traditional epithet attached to the chief of the Gordon clan.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was created a [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Order_of_the_Thistle Knight of the Thistle],  [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_Knights_and_Ladies_of_the_Thistle 29 May 1687],
2 CONT
2 CONT He raised the [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/92nd_(Gordon_Highlanders)_Regiment_of_Foot 92nd (Gordon Highlanders) Regiment of Foot] in 1794 for the French Revolutionary Wars. He was responsible for establishing the new village of F
2 CONC ochabers as well as those of Tomintoul and Portgordon in Banffshire. He is also credited as the founder of the Gordon Setter breed of dog, having popularised a 200-year-old breed during the 18th century and then formalised its bre
2 CONC ed standard in 1820.
