1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>DRUMMOND OF LOGIEALMOND, SIR WILLIAM JAMES CHARLES MARIA</strong>. ?-29/03/1828. Ref: 448. Male.
2 CONT *Titles and British Honours: Knight (1803), PC(1801).
2 CONT *Place of Birth: Perthshire.
2 CONT *Place of Death: Rome, Italy.
2 CONT *Profession: Scholar, Diplomat.
2 CONT *Appointments Held: MP 1795-6, St Mawes, 1796-1802 Lostwithiel; 1801 Envoy Extraordinary to the Court of Naples; 1803 Ambasssador to the Ottoman Court; 1806-9 Envoy to the Court of Naples; 1809-resided in London.
2 CONT *Undergraduate Studies: Oxford University.
2 CONT *Postgraduate Studies: DCL(Oxon 1810).
2 CONT *Father: John Drummond, Perth.
2 CONT *References: DNB 16, 1888, 51; Anderson 2, 67-8; Irving 111; Shapin 142.
2 CONT *Memberships: FRS (1799), Highland Society.
2 CONT *Date of Election: 22/01/1798.
2 CONT *Proposers: Dugald Stewart, Alexander Keith, John Playfair (Minute 08/01/1798 NLS Acc10,000/4 & Acc 10,000/12).
2 CONT *Notes: Born c.1770.
2 CONT *Fellow Type: OF.
