1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Name:	Sosanah Bostick
2 CONT [Rosannah Bostick]
2 CONT [Rosanah Bostick]
2 CONT [Rosannah Murray Bostick]
2 CONT Gender:	Female
2 CONT Race:	White
2 CONT Age:	67
2 CONT Birth Year:	abt 1783
2 CONT Birthplace:	North Carolina
2 CONT Home in 1850:	Subdivision 2, Lincoln, Tennessee, USA
2 CONT Cannot Read, Write:	Yes
2 CONT Line Number:	41
2 CONT Dwelling Number:	1363
2 CONT Family Number:	1363
2 CONT Household Members	Age
2 CONT Charles D Bostick 31  https://www.geni.com/people/Chesley-Bostick/6000000185507648087?through=6000000078771722544
2 CONT Frances Bostick 24
2 CONT William Bostick 6
2 CONT Elizabeth Bostick 4
2 CONT Nathan A Bostick 2  https://www.geni.com/people/Nathaniel-Bostick/6000000185509380929?through=6000000078771722544
2 CONT Mathew D Bostick 26  https://www.geni.com/people/Matthew-Bostick/6000000185508423076?through=6000000078771722544
2 CONT Mary Bostick 21
2 CONT '''Sosanah Bostick	67'''  https://www.geni.com/people/Rosannah-Hale-Bostic/6000000078771722544
2 CONT * https://www.ancestry.com/discoveryui-content/view/6336033:8054?ssrc=pt&tid=43552172&pid=182390318020
2 CONT
2 CONT Note:
2 CONT "Sosanah" Bostick is believed to have been Rosannah Murray Bostick, widow of Floyd Bostick. 
2 CONT The two older male Bosticks in this household: Charles D. and Matthew D. are believed to have been younger sons of Rosannah and Floyd.  
2 CONT The two older women: Frances and Mary are believed to have been daughters-in-law, and wives of the two sons.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Floyd Bostick married Rosannah Murray on June 12 1817 in Blount Co., TN. She was probably the same woman that married Thomas Hail (Hale) on April 23, 1801 in Blount Co., TN. She was listed as Rossana Denne in the marriage record.
2 CONT Rosanna named one of her sons, Matthew Denny Bostick. There were three women with the maiden name of Denney that married around the same time in Blount Co., TN.
2 CONT Pressey Denney married David Cunningham on January 13, 1798.Mary Denney married Miles Cunningham on May 22, 1797.Patsy Denny married Benjamin Stigall on August 20, 1802.
2 CONT The Blount, Tennessee Tax Roll in 1801 listed Matthew Denning, David Cunningham and Miles Cunningham. (More research is needed for Matthew Denning. The spelling may be incorrect and the last name was actually "Denney". David and M
2 CONC iles Cunningham married Pressey and Mary Denney.)
2 CONT August 24, 1807: Rosannah received administrator bond for estate of Thomas Hail; signed James Beard and James Gillespie
2 CONT 1813: Floyd Bostick witnessed a deed from Luke Hail to John McCool for 155 acres. The land was part of a land grant to Luke and Thomas Hail for 315 acres.
2 CONT It appears that Thomas Hale died by August 24 1807. Floyd Bostick was in Blount County, Tennessee by 1805 when he wrote a letter to the Court of Prince Edward Co., VA.
2 CONT Rosannah Denney (spelled Denne in the marriage record to Thomas Hail) may have married a Murray between 1807 and 1817, when she married Floyd Bostick.
2 CONT Matthew Denney Bostick made application for a Civil War claim in Madison County, AL on August 29, 1873. A deposition was made by William Hale, age 65. He stated that he was a half brother to Matthew D. Bostic. Hale's oldest son wa
2 CONC s named Thomas and his second daughter was named Rosannah.
2 CONT
2 CONT This needs to be proven by record. However, if this is correct, Rosannah's maiden name was Denney.
2 CONT '''The assumption is....Rosannah Denne (Denney) married Thomas Hale in 1801.Rosannah married a Murray after the death of Thomas Hale.Rosannah married Floyd Bostick in 1817.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Murray-19371 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:21:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Wife of Floyd Bostick and mother of Alfred, Ann, Nathaniel, Chesley Butler, and Matthew Denny Bostick, as well as son William Hail.
2 CONT
2 CONT Rosannah married her husband Floyd on June 11, 1817, in Blount County, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Before Rosannah was married to Floyd, she married Thomas Hail in Blount County, Tennessee, on April 23, 1801. 
2 CONT Thomas Hail passed on in 1807. 
2 CONT She had a son with Thomas Hail, William Hail.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/127657251/rosannah-denne-bostick Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:23:16 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Lincoln, Lincoln, Tennessee, United States - 1850
