1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Alternate Data, omitted during merge of 12/1/09:
2 CONT
2 CONT Last  Name: Spencer-Churchill
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Lady Susan Stewart was born on 10 April 1767.1 She was the daughter of John Stewart, 7th Earl of Galloway and Anne Dashwood. She married George Spencer-Churchill, 5th Duke of Marlborough, son of George Spencer, 4th Duke of Marlbor
2 CONC ough and Lady Caroline Russell, on 15 September 1791 at St. James's, London, England.1 She died on 2 April 1841 at age 73 at Park Lane, Mayfair, London, England.1 Her will was probated in May 1841.1
2 CONT      As a result of her marriage, Lady Susan Stewart was styled as Marchioness of Blandford on 15 September 1791. From 15 September 1791, her married name became Spencer-Churchill. As a result of her marriage, Lady Susan Stewart w
2 CONC as styled as Duchess of Marlborough on 29 January 1817. Children of Lady Susan Stewart and George Spencer-Churchill, 5th Duke of Marlborough George Spencer-Churchill, 6th Duke of Marlborough+ b. 27 Dec 1793, d. 1 Jul 1857.1 Lord C
2 CONC harles Spencer-Churchill+ b. 3 Dec 1794, d. 28 Apr 1840.2 Reverend Lord George Henry Spencer-Churchill b. 18 May 1796, d. 1828.2
2 CONT
2 CONT Citations
2 CONT
