2 CONT      Lady Susan Stewart was born on 10 April 1767.1 She was the daughter of John Stewart, 7th Earl of Galloway and Anne Dashwood. She married George Spencer-Churchill, 5th Duke of Marlborough, son of George Spencer, 4th Duke of Ma
2 CONC rlborough and Lady Caroline Russell, on 15 September 1791 at St. James's, London, England.1 She died on 2 April 1841 at age 73 at Park Lane, Mayfair, London, England.1 Her will was probated in May 1841.1
2 CONT      As a result of her marriage, Lady Susan Stewart was styled as Marchioness of Blandford on 15 September 1791. From 15 September 1791, her married name became Spencer-Churchill. As a result of her marriage, Lady Susan Stewart w
2 CONC as styled as Duchess of Marlborough on 29 January 1817. Children of Lady Susan Stewart and George Spencer-Churchill, 5th Duke of Marlborough George Spencer-Churchill, 6th Duke of Marlborough+1 b. 27 Dec 1793, d. 1 Jul 1857 Lord Ch
2 CONC arles Spencer-Churchill+2 b. 3 Dec 1794, d. 28 Apr 1840 Reverend Lord George Henry Spencer-Churchill2 b. 18 May 1796, d. 1828 Citations [S6] G.E. Cokayne; with Vicary Gibbs, H.A. Doubleday, Geoffrey H. White, Duncan Warrand and Lo
2 CONC rd Howard de Walden, editors, The Complete Peerage of England, Scotland, Ireland, Great Britain and the United Kingdom, Extant, Extinct or Dormant, new ed., 13 volumes in 14 (1910-1959; reprint in 6 volumes, Gloucester, U.K.: Alan
