2 CONT Early life and family
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Richard Stewart was born on 5 May 1782, the fifth surviving son of John Stewart, 7th Earl of Galloway, and his second wife, Anne Dashwood, daughter of Sir James Dashwood, 2nd Baronet. He was educated at Charterhouse. He mar
2 CONC ried the Honourable Katherine Charteris, daughter of Francis Charteris, Lord Elcho. One of his children, Jane Francis Clinton Stewart, went on to marry her first cousin, George Spencer-Churchill, 6th Duke of Marlborough, son of Ge
2 CONC orge Spencer-Churchill, 5th Duke of Marlborough, and Lady Susan Stewart.
2 CONT
2 CONT Career
2 CONT
2 CONT He represented Wigtown Burghs from 1806 to 1809.
