2 CONT '''From [https://books.google.co.uk/books?id=g6k3ftoWSSAC&pg=PA326&lpg=PA326&dq=%22Thomas+Graham%22+%22Valparaiso%22&source=bl&ots=JFHYTKaslw&sig=ACfU3U35djkvXqUEZPxwr-CsbQVmK8-pUw&hl=en&sa=X&ved=2ahUKEwiAjtOShLHqAhVgQEEAHfI9A5EQ6
2 CONC AEwAnoECGIQAQ#v=onepage&q=%22Thomas%20Graham%22%20%22Valparaiso%22&f=false Chile: The Bradt Travel Guide - Tim Burford]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The Museo Lord Cochrane is a single-storey house built in 1841 on part of what was the Castillo San José, built in 1682. Thomas Graham, commander of the British frigate Doris, died at sea and was buried in the Castillo in 1822; hi
2 CONC s widow Mary Graham, who was accompanying him, lived for a while in El Almendral, the area just east of the old town of Valparaíso and entertained Lord Cochrane and O'Higgins. Her account of Chile, published in 1824, provides a wo
2 CONC nderful picture of the country as it emerged from colonial rule.
