2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew Morton Carr of Saville House, Twickenham, Middlesex; born in London 17 July 1799, baptised at St. Pancras', London, 17 August 1799; educated at Harrow and at [Peterhouse], Cambridge, B.A. 1820 ; Barrister-at-Law of Gray's I
2 CONC nn 16 May 1827, Solicitor of Excise of Scotland 1827, and of England and Scotland 1844-49; married firstly at [Strathtyrum], Fife, 12 July 1830, Caroline Aeneas Mackay Graham, 13th daughter of Robert Graham of Fintry, Fife, who di
2 CONC ed 26 May 1826, and was buried at St. John-the-Evangelist's, Edinburgh, 30 May 1826. He died at Saville House, Twickenham, 17 September 1852, buried at Teddington, Middlesex, 21 September 1852. Will dated 18 December 1845, proved 
2 CONC 8 November 1852, by William Cornwall, one of the Executors.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Married to] Emily Caroline Fortescue, 4th daughter of Major-General Lord Robert Kerr, K.H., Secretary of the Honourable Order of the Thistle, by Mary his wife, daughter of Rev. Edmund Gilbert of Windsor House, Cornwall;  born at 
2 CONC Dalhousie Castle, Forfarshire [now Angus], 27 June 1817; married at Caroline Park, Edinburgh, 17 July 1841 (marriage registered at St. John's, Edinburgh); died at 89 St. George's Square, London, 19 April 1893, buried at  Teddingto
2 CONC n Cemetery 24 April 1893. Will dated 17 January 1873, proved 31 May 1893, by Andrew Mark Carr, the son, the Executors 2nd wife. 
2 CONT
