3 CTRY Guernsey
1 TITL Maj. Gen.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Possible merge opportunity? half brother of same name varying birth dates.
2 CONT
2 CONT == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT <strong>Macleod of Macleod, Norman</strong>. 04/03/1754-?. Ref: 990. Male.
2 CONT * Titles and British Honours: Major General.
2 CONT * Place of Birth: Brodie House, Nairn.
2 CONT * Place of Death: Guernsey.
2 CONT * Profession: Soldier, Politician.
2 CONT * Appointments Held: Enlisted 1774, 42nd Regiment, Malabar, India; 1786, 73rd Regiment, 1794 Major-General; MP 1790-6 Inverness-shire.
2 CONT * Undergraduate Studies: St Andrews, Oxford University.
2 CONT * Father: John MacLeod, 19th Laird of MacLeod.
2 CONT * Other Family: Nephew of John Hill FRSE 1747-1805.
2 CONT * References: Shapin 317; S Devlin-Thorp Scotland's Cultural Heritage, 2, 1981, 60.
2 CONT * Memberships: FRS (1791), Highland Society.
2 CONT * Date of Election: 28/06/1790.
2 CONT * Proposers: John Hill, Andrew Duncan, James Hutton (Literary Section Minute 18/01/1790 NLS Acc10,000/3).
2 CONT * Notes: Died August 1801.
2 CONT * Fellow Type: OF.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Waterston, Charles D; Macmillan Shearer, A (July 2006). [http://www.royalsoced.org.uk/cms/files/fellows/biographical_index/fells_indexp2.pdf Biographical index of former fellows of the Royal Society of Edinburgh, 1783-200
2 CONC 2]: Biographical Index. II. Edinburgh: The Royal Society of Edinburgh. ISBN 978-0-902198-84-5. page 606
2 CONT
2 CONT == Other References ==
2 CONT * [http://archive.org/stream/historyofmacleod00mack#page/154/mode/2up History of the Macleods with genealogies of the principal families of the name]; Alexander Mackenzie; 1889; page 155-182
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT "Major General Norman Macleod" 23rd Chief of Clan Macleod
2 CONT Here are some resources about the son of John Macleod and Amelia Brodie. 
2 CONT
2 CONT General Norman Macleod, 23rd Chief.
2 CONT #1: "Norman Macleod was the 23rd Chief of Clan Macleod, referred to as 'The General'. He was the son of John Macleod and Amelia Brodie." It is a British source.  https://www.britishempire.co.uk/forces/armyunits/britishinfantry/42.
2 CONC ..
2 CONT
2 CONT #2: Another well respected source is Clan MacFarlane and associated clans genealogy site. They list him similarly as "Gen. Norman MacLeod, 23rd Chief"  https://www.clanmacfarlanegenealogy.info/genealogy/TNGWebsite/getpe...
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
