1 NAME Elizabeth Pringle MacLean (MacLeod)
1 SEX F
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Elizabeth Pringle MacLeod [719] (Jessie MacDonald 3, James Macdonald of 2, Alexander Old Kingsburgh 1).
2 CONT Elizabeth married Rev. Roderick MacLean Ostal [723] [MRIN: 252]. Roderick was born in 1772 in Osdal, Dunvegan, Isle of Skye, Scotland and died on 4 Jun 1854 in Drimsdale, South Uist, Scotland, aged 82.
2 CONT
2 CONT Biography
2 CONT Roderick was born on Skye in 1772, the son of Donald MacLean, 4th of Kinloch. He was educated at King's College, Aberdeen and the University of Edinburgh (MA 1797). He served as schoolmaster at Portree in 1800. Rev. Roderick MacLe
2 CONC an was licensed by the presbytery of Skye December 2, 1801. He was an ordained missionary at Hallin-in-Waternish on April 8, 1807. He moved to Carinish, North Uist, about1810. In 1818 he was appointed Justice of the Peace and Depu
2 CONC ty Lieutenant in 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT The child from this marriage was:
2 CONT
2 CONT i. Charles MacLean [2474] was born on 2 Feb 1818 in Grogarry, South Uist, Outer Hebrides, Scotland and
2 CONT died on 21 Nov 1906 in Milton, South Uist, Scotland, aged 88.
