1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Pringle, Baronet [S. 1683], of Stichell</strong>, 2d but 1st surv. s. and h., b. there 20 Jan. 1784; Captain 12th Light Dragoons, having been ten years in that regiment ; suc. to the Baronetcy, 7 April 1809. He m
2 CONC . firstly, 2 June 1809, Emilia Anne, 2d da. of his maternal uncle, Lieut.-Gen. Norman Macleod, of Macleod, by his 2d wife, Sarah, da. of N. Stackhouse, " Second in Council " at Bombay. She d. 22 Feb. 1830, at Stichell. He m. secon
2 CONC dly, 10 Oct. 1831, at Langton, co. Berwick, Elizabeth Maitland, 1st da. of John (Campbell), 1st Marquess of Breadaleane, by Mary Turner, da. and coheir of David Gavin, of Langton aforesaid. He d. s.p.m.s., at Langton, 15 June 1869
2 CONC , aged about 85. His widow, who was b. 25 July 1794, d. 17 Feb. 1878, at Langton, aged 83."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n337/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 319
