1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir Norman Pringle, Baronet [S. 1683]</strong>, br. and h. male, b. 22 July 1787, at Edinburgh ; second-Lieut. 21st Fusiliers, 1804 ; served in Sicily, 1806 ; in Egypt, 1807 ; at the defence of Scylla Castle, 1808 ; in Sp
2 CONC ain, with the Catalonian army, 1812 ; in Italy, 1814, being at the capture of Genoa ; also in North America, being in the actions of Baltimore, New Orleans, etc. ; became Major 21st Fusiliers in 1814, retiring in 1815 ; was Consul
2 CONC  at Stockholm, 1846-57, and at Dunkirk, 1857, till death in 1870; suc. to the Baronetcy (in his 83d year) 15 June 1869, but not, apparently, to the estates. He ire., 17 Jan. 1826, at Alderston, in Scotland, Anne, 1st da. of Robert
2 CONC  Steuart of Alderston. He d. 17 April 1870, aged 82, at the British Consulate, Dunkirk. His widow d. 4 Aug. 1883, at 85 St. George's Road, Pimlico."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524408#page/n337/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1904; Vol. IV; page 319-320
