1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widow
2 CONC s: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;I
2 CONC n the early 1800s, Canada had relied on England for shipments of manufactured goods such as shoes, ale, ironworks and furniture. The 1850s and 60s saw a massive explosion in the economy, and many Londoners (new and established) de
2 CONC cided that they wanted to try their own hands at economic endeavours. The Kingsmills &ndash; whose famed department store operated in London for 148 years &ndash; were one of these families./p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-botto
2 CONC m: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; backgro
2 CONC und-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;Thomas was born in Tipperary, Ireland 
2 CONC on ap ril 6, 1840, and came to North America as an immigrant with his wife Anne in 1860. They settled in London in 1864 and, as many will recall, opened a dry goods shop called Kingsmill&rsquo;s on Dundas Street. He rented the bui
2 CONC lding from John Walsingham Cooke Meredith for a grand total of $400 per year. Thomas, Anne, and their six children lived at 862 Ridout Street North, a popular part of town for those in (or aspiring to be in) London&rsquo;s high so
2 CONC ciety./p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans:
2 CONC  2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: 
2 CONC initial;&nbsp;/p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; 
2 CONC orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration
2 CONC -color: initial;Many said that Thomas was born for a life of service. He possessed superior knowledge about cloth and fabric, and spent years of his life travelling to Europe and back by boat to personally purchase cloth for his L
2 CONC ondon, Ontario customers. He was said to have crossed the Atlantic Ocean 140 for this purpose./p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px;
2 CONC  text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal;
2 CONC  -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;More than stellar customer service, Kingsmill&rsquo;s store was one of the first in London to introduce a fair price system. Due to th
2 CONC e fact that London was still a fairly new community in the 1860s, many businesses still operated on a barter system, which was prone to haggling and compromising. Thomas ensured that all of his goods were marked with one price onl
2 CONC y, in plain figures &ndash; a system which soon became the norm in London. This was certainly a mark of London&rsquo;s transition from a pioneer town to a bustling city./p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family
2 CONC : Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; t
2 CONC ext-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;Besides being one of London&rsquo;s most prominent business
2 CONC men, Thomas also served as a city alderman from 1873-1874, was active in creating London&rsquo;s first water commission, and was largely responsible for erecting Blackfriar&rsquo;s Bridge &ndash; the first still arch to span the T
2 CONC hames &ndash; near his Ridout Street home./p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #
2 CONC b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-sty
2 CONC le: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;Thomas passed away in 1915 of bladder disease, and it was then that another dramatic &ndash; and scandalous &ndash; feature of his life was revealed. Since his wife Anne had already pass
2 CONC ed away, he left his estate to his children. Before the funds could be distributed, span&nbsp;/spanem style=font-style: italic;anotherspan&nbsp;/span/emMrs. Kingsmill stepped forward claiming to be Thomas&rsquo; wife, and she and 
2 CONC her three children rightfully entitled to a share of the estate. The details came out through a court case in which the 2sup style=font-size: 12px; vertical-align: baseline; position: relative; line-height: 0; top: -0.5em;nd/supsp
2 CONC an&nbsp;/spanMrs. Kingsmill, born Margaret Gill, contested Thomas&rsquo; will. She was living in England when she aNew South Walesered a newspaper ad and became Mr. Kingsmill&rsquo;s employee in 1883, eventually marryinghim in Can
2 CONC ada in &rsquo;84 and returning to live in England. She was not notified that Thomas was already married until after the wedding. Thomas would spend most of the year in London, Ontario with Anne, but would live with Margaret while 
2 CONC on his cloth-buying business trips to England. Margaret and Thomas had 3 children &ndash; Percy, Irene, and Vernon &ndash; who came to Canada in 1910 and took up residence in the first Kingsmill house when Thomas died. As one may 
2 CONC expect, this did not go over well. It seems as if Canadians&rsquo; new sense of themselves as global citizens had more than a fewunexpected benefits&hellip;/p p style=font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 1.6em; font-family: Vollkorn, s
2 CONC erif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: normal; color: #b9b3b0; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; background-color: #3f3f3f; text-indent: 0
2 CONC px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;Despite this scandal and the bout of bad feeling that followed, the King
2 CONC smill family continued to play a prominent role in London society./p p style=text-align: left; dir=ltr&nbsp;/p p style=font-size: 16px; font-family: 'Open Sans', Arial, sans-serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-to
2 CONC p: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: 100; color: #4d4d4d; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 25px; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; fon
2 CONC t-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;n his lifetime, Thomas Frazer Kingsmill crossed the Atlantic more than 140 times, travelling frequently to supp
2 CONC liers&rsquo; factories and mills in England and Europe to buy table linens, woollens and other textiles to supply his London store with the latest in stylish, quality goods./p p style=font-size: 16px; font-family: 'Open Sans', Ari
2 CONC al, sans-serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: 100; color: #4d4d4d; font-style: normal; orphans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 25px; background-colo
2 CONC r: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal;-webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; text-decoration-color: initial;Kingsmill&rsquo;s father opened a dry goods bus
2 CONC iness in the 1830s in County Tipperary, Ireland, but it failed, a casualty of economic hardship, epidemic, and famine. Thomas Frazer Kingsmill left school and ap prenticed himself to another dry goods merchant. In 1858, he and his
2 CONC  wife, Annie, emigrated to the United States, but the poor import trade resulting from the American Civil War forced them to move again in 1863 to Toronto, where Kingsmill found employment with W.A. Murray &amp; Co. Two years late
2 CONC r he became manager of Murray&rsquo;s London branch. When Kingsmill began his own business in 1865 at 130 Dundas Street, he advertised heavily in the local papers and introduced a one-price policy,to the relief of shoppers weary o
2 CONC f the barter system./p p style=font-size: 16px; font-family: 'Open Sans', Arial, sans-serif; white-space: normal; word-spacing: 0px; margin-top: 0px; text-transform: none; font-weight: 100; color: #4d4d4d; font-style: normal; orph
2 CONC ans: 2; widows: 2; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 25px; background-color: #ffffff; text-indent: 0px; font-variant-ligatures: normal; font-variant-caps: normal; -webkit-text-stroke-width: 0px; text-decoration-style: initial; 
2 CONC text-decoration-color: initial;In 1875, he acquired the adjoining property and built the store through to Carling Street. A carpet warehouse was added in 1884. In its early years, Kingsmill&rsquo;s specialized in cashmeres, embroi
2 CONC dered handkerchiefs, gloves, carpets, and linens. Its product range was later expanded to include china, furniture, housewares, and lamps. The store expanded again in 1904./p
