1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was a farmer and a manufacturer of goods in 1820, a a blacksmith in 1850, and a slave owner in several census records for 1810, 1820, 1830 & 1840. Richard and Mary were married 58 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Conflicting info: Marriage to Mary Margaret "Molly" Lake on November 5, 1796 in Fauquier County, Virginia
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=67249043
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage record revealed Richard Cross and Molly Lake married on March 8, 1796 in Fauquier County, Virginia.  Richard was twenty-four and Margaret was eighteen when they were married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1810 census revealed that they lived in Harrison County, Virginia. Household members: Richard Cross (26-44), Margaret (26-44), Nimrod and one male (under 10), Susannah & one female (10-15), Nancy (under 10) and one slave.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1820 census revealed that he was a farmer and a manufacturer of goods. Household members: Richard Cross (45 & up), Margaret (26-44), Nimrod (10-15), Susannah (19-23), Nancy & three females (under 10) and three slaves.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1830 census revealed household members: Richard Cross (50-59), Margaret (50-59), one male (20-29), two females (10-14), Jane (5-9), two female slaves (24 & up), one female slave (10-23) and five slaves (under 10). 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1840 census revealed Richard was employed in manufacturer of goods and four household members were employed in agriculture. Household members: Richard Cross (60-69), Margaret (50-59), two male slaves (10-23), one male slave (u
2 CONC nder 10), one female slave (24-35), one female slave (10-23) and one female slave (under 10).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 census revealed Richard was a blacksmith and their real estate value was $900. They were living in District 63, Taylor County, Virginia. They were born in Tennessee and could not read or write. Household members: Richard 
2 CONC Cross (79) and Mary (76).
2 CONT
2 CONT Their known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah Cross (Bailey)(b.1797 d.1872) Female Cross (b. bet.1798-1800) Male Cross (b. bet.1801-1809) Nimrod Cross (b.1804 d.1888) Nancy Cross (Davis)(b.1810 d.1890) Female Cross (b. bet.1815-1820) Female Cross (b. bet.1815-1820) J
2 CONC ane A. Cross (Hustead)(b.1821) 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had been married fifty-eight years when Richard died on April 15, 1854 in Taylor, (West) Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard lived to age 82.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Richard Cross BIRTH	4 Feb 1772 Virginia, USA DEATH	15 Apr 1854 (aged 82) Virginia, USA BURIAL	Unknown
2 CONT
