2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 DEC 1859
2 PLAC Gordon's Ferry, TN
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://gordonhouse.50megs.com/photo.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Dolley Cross Gordon married the Captain in 1794 & lived to be 81 passing away in 1859. She was a successful business woman operating the Duck River Ferry and Trading Post while her husband was away on his excursions.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.msa.md.gov/megafile/msa/speccol/sc3500/sc3520/002100/002185/notes/steele.dir/parsonstech/genealogy/trees/jgordon/d1329.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT During his many absences, Dolly Cross Gordon ran the establishment at Gordon's Ferry, as she would continue to do after his early death. A vital, remarkable woman, she matched her husband in abilities and reputation. There is no k
2 CONC nown portrait of John Gordon, but a miniature of Dolly Cross survives, in my possession. He was married to Dorothea (Dolly) Cross on Jul 15 1794 in Nashville, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT  Children were:
2 CONT
2 CONT child i. John Gordon was born in 1795 in Nashville, Tennessee. He died about 1844 in Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT child ii. Fielding Lewis Gordon was born about 1797 in Nashville, Tennessee. He died in 1835 in St. Louis, Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT child iii. Captain William Gordon was born in 1798 in Nashville, Tennessee. He died after 1845.
2 CONT
2 CONT child iv. Major Bolling Gordon was born in 1800 in Nashville, Tennessee. He died on Dec 10 1880 in "Cottage Hill" Hickman County, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT child16 v. Major Powhatan Gordon.
2 CONT
2 CONT child vi. Mary Ann Gordon was born in 1807. She died about 1845.
2 CONT
2 CONT child vii. Anna "Nancy" Gordon was born about 1809 in Gordon's Ferry, Tennessee. She died Young.
2 CONT
2 CONT child viii. Dorothy "Dolly" Gordon was born on Nov 29 1811 in Gordon's Ferry, Tennessee. She died on Dec 4 1880 in Trenton, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT child ix. Andrew Gordon was born in 1813 in Gordon's Ferry, Tennessee. He died on Aug 2 1888.
2 CONT
2 CONT child x. Lieutenant Richard Cross Gordon was born on Jan 10 1817 in Gordon's Ferry, Tennessee. He died on Nov 20 1863.
2 CONT
2 CONT child xi. Louisa Pocahontas Gordon was born on Feb 19 1819 in Gordon's Ferry, Tennessee. She died on Jul 13 1857 in Nashville, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://www.tnportraits.org/gordon-dorothea-dolly-cross.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Notes:	Subject (1779-1859) was married to John Gordon, "Captain of the Spies" for Andrew Jackson. When he was in Florida with Jackson, Dolly managed their trading post on the Natchez Trace. Their residence on the Trace, known as "
2 CONC Gordon House," is still there at mile marker 407.7. John Gordon was also the first postmaster in Nashville.
