1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/126930414/ethelbert-algernon-coleman
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Magazine of Albermarle County History - Volume 44 - 1986
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ethelbert Algernon Coleman was born at Woodlawn in Halifax County, Virginia on 12-Feb-1812, ninth child of the twelve children of Colonel Henry Embry Coleman and Anne Gordon."
2 CONT
2 CONT Misc notes from RootsWeb:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Ethelbert Algernon Coleman received his A.B. degree from Hampden-Sydney College in 1830, after which he studied medicine at the University of Virginia and the University of Pennsylvania, where he graduated in 1833. He was first m
2 CONC arried to Mary Elizabeth Sims at "Black Walnut." She died at their home, "Rose Hill" and is buried at "Black Walnut." Both homes being in Halifax County, Virginia. He was married secondly at "Riverside" to Martha Frances Ragsdale.
2 CONC  She was the daughter of Nathaniel and Ann Boswell Ragsdale of "Riverside." Dr and Mrs Coleman, parents of 12 children, made their home at "Rose Hill" until 1841, when it was replaced by the mansion they called "Creekside." Mrs Co
2 CONC leman is buried with her husband at Grace Episcopal Church Cemetery, News Ferry, Halifax County, Virginia. Mr Coleman attended Hampden-Sydney College with his friend, George W Dame, who later became the first rector of The Episcop
2 CONC al Church of the Epiphany in Danville, Virginia."
2 CONT --------------------
