1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bostick-335 WikiTree Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:21:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred was the first-born child of Floyd and Rosannah Murray Bostick, and was the brother of Ann, Chesley Butler, Nathaniel, and Matthew Denny Bostick. He married Elizabeth Hickman on June 1, 1837, in Franklin County, Tennessee. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred served in the Army, entering around 1837 in Fayetteville, Tennessee. He served as a Private for six months in Captain Robert's Company, 1st Regiment of General Armstrong's Brigade of Mounted Eagle Volunteers of the Tennesse
2 CONC e Militia. According to Claims of Tennessee Volunteers, he was discharged on January 17, 1837 in New Orleans, Louisiana.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred and Elizabeth were parents to Mary Jane, George, William Berry, Elizabeth, Joshua Hickman, Francis Asbury, Martha Carolyn, Clarinda, and John R. Bostick.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred had three sons that fought on the Union side of the Civil War- Francis Asbury (died while in service), Josuah, and William. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Alfred died July 23, 1852, in Perry County, Arkansas.
