1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Bostick-473 WikiTree Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:21:10 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT A TRIBUTE TO MY GREAT-GREAT GRANDFATHER NATHANIEL
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel Alexander Bostick was born in Tennessee to Floyd and Rosannah Murray Bostick in 1819. He was the sibling of Alfred, Ann, Chesley Butler, and Matthew Denny Bostick. He married Caroline Stovall, daughter of Ancel Manley St
2 CONC ovall and Anna Rich Stovall, on July 18, 1841 in Franklin County, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel and Caroline had several children. They had twin sons, Ancel Chesley and George (Ancil Chesley "A.C." is my great grandfather, and he was named Ancil after his Mother Caroline's father, Ancil Stovall). In addition, they 
2 CONC had the following children: John Floyd,  Rose Anna, Elizabeth, Cyntha, Thomas "Tommie" Emaline (female), Robert Lee (who was a female named after General Robert E. Lee, and whose nieces & nephews called "Aunt Bob"),  Agatmyu, Will
2 CONC iam,  and Beauregard (who later changed his name to Burie). Agatmyu, Cyntha and William are buried along with their father Nathaniel at Damron Cemetery. Rose Anna and Burie are buried at Stateline (Bostick) Cemetery in Plevna, Mad
2 CONC ison County, Alabama, with their mother,  Nathaniel's wife, Caroline Stovall Bostick.
2 CONT
2 CONT Nathaniel was a Lieutenant in the Confederate Army under the command of Captain F. Rice of the Alabama Volunteer Company. He was discharged in 1862.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1883, after Nathaniel's passing on,  Caroline filed for a widow's pension in Madison County, Alabama, and it was granted to her.
2 CONT
2 CONT Thank you Granddaddy for serving your country, and may we meet in Heaven one day!
2 CONT
2 CONT Remembering you with love,
2 CONT
2 CONT Your great-great-granddaughter Kimberly* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/96421030/nathaniel-alexander-bostick Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:23
2 CONC :16 UTC''
