1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Golden Fleece - Knights: Spanish Branch===
2 CONT * Full name - Italian: - '''Carlo Tito Francesco Giuseppe'''
2 CONT * [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carlo,_Duke_of_Calabria '''Carlo Tito Francesco Giuseppe''']
2 CONT * Carlo, Duke of Calabria
2 CONT
2 CONT * Italian: - Carlo Tito Francesco Giuseppe
2 CONT * House - 	House of Bourbon
2 CONT * Father -	Ferdinand IV of Naples
2 CONT * Mother - 	Maria Carolina of Austria
2 CONT * Born - 4 January 1775, Caserta Palace, Kingdom of Naples
2 CONT * Died -17 December 1778 (aged 3),  Caserta Palace, Kingdom of Naples
2 CONT * Burial - Basilica of Santa Chiara, Naples
2 CONT * Religion - Roman Catholic
2 CONT * Carlo of Naples and Sicily (Italian: Carlo Tito Francesco Giuseppe; 4 January 1775 – 17 December 1778) was a Prince of Naples and Sicily and Duke of Calabria. He died in infancy of smallpox.
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT * Born at the Caserta Palace[1] near Naples, he was created Duke of Calabria at birth as the heir apparent to his father's throne. His mother was a daughter of Empress Maria Theresa and thus sister of Marie Antoinette.
2 CONT * A member of the House of Bourbon, he was a prince of Naples and Sicily by birth. He was the hereditary prince of Naples.[1] His birth allowed his mother to have a place in the Council of State, part of his parents' marriage cont
2 CONC ract.
2 CONT * Carlo died of smallpox[2] aged 3. Two of his younger siblings would die of smallpox also the said Princess Maria Cristina Amelia who caught it from Prince Giuseppe the two dying within a week of each other.
2 CONT * He was buried at the Church of Santa Chiara in Naples.
2 CONT ===Titles and styles===
2 CONT * 4 January 1775 – 17 December 1778 His Royal Highness Don Carlo, Duke of Calabria, Hereditary Prince of Naples and Sicily
