2 CONT THE   MARRIAGES OF FERDINAND VII (WIKIPEDIA)
2 CONT
2 CONT Ferdinand VII was married four times. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1802, he married his first cousin Princess Maria Antonia of Naples and Sicily (1784–1806), daughter of Ferdinand I of the Two Sicilies and Marie Caroline of Austria. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There were no children, because her two pregnancies (in 1804 and 1805) both ended in miscarriages.
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~ In 1816, Ferdinand married his niece Maria Isabel of Portugal (1797–1818), daughter of his older sister Carlota Joaquina and John VI of Portugal. She bore him two daughters, the first of whom lived only five months and t
2 CONC he second of whom was stillborn. ~~~~~~~~~ In 20 October 1819, in Madrid, Ferdinand married Princess Maria Josepha Amalia of Saxony (1803–1829), daughter of Maximilian, Prince of Saxony, and Caroline of Parma. No children were bor
2 CONC n from this marriage. ~~~~~~~~ Lastly, on 27 May 1829, Ferdinand married another niece, Maria Christina of the Two Sicilies (1806–1878), daughter of his younger sister Maria Isabella of Spain and Francis I of the Two Sicilies. She
2 CONC  bore him two surviving daughters, the older of whom succeeded Ferdinand upon his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT 6 daughters total including one stillborn (Where did I get that number 6? It has to be wrong). 
2 CONT
2 CONT (It appears Ferdinand, at the time of his death had one daughter, the one that succeeded him upon his death.
