1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis_Antoine,_Duke_of_Angouleme ''[46 languages]''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Louis Antoine of France, Duke of Angoulême''', sometimes known as '''Louis XIX''' (6 August 1775 – 3 June 1844), was the elder son of Charles X of France and the last Dauphin of France from 1824 to 1830. He was disputedly King 
2 CONC of France and Navarre for less than 20 minutes as '''Louis XIX''' before he himself abdicated, due to his father's abdication during the July Revolution in 1830. He never reigned over the country, but after his father's death in 1
2 CONC 836, he was the legitimist pretender to the French throne.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a petit-fils de France at birth, and was initially known as Louis Antoine d'Artois. After his father's accession to the throne, he became Dauphin de France, and his surname changed to de France, following the royal custom f
2 CONC or princes with such rank.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Plate-Duke_of_Angouleme-IMG_8678-white.jpg/220px-Plate-Duke_of_Angouleme-IMG_8678-white.jpg|right|80px}}
