2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Atholl Bannatyne Murray-Macgregor, Baronet [1795]</strong>, of Clangregor Castle, 1st s. and h., b. 20 Jan. 1810; suc. to the Baronetcy, 14 June 1841 ; President of the Virgin Islands, 1860. He m, 14 Nov. 1833, a
2 CONC t Sr James', Westm., Mary Charlotte, 3d and yst. da. and coheir of Rear-Admiral Sir Thomas Masterman Hardy, Baronet (so cr. 1806), G.CB., Governor of Greenwich Hospital (d. 20 Sep. 1839), by Louisa Emily Anne, da. of Admiral the H
2 CONC on. Sir George Cranfield Berkeley, G C.B., yr. s. of the 4th Earl of Berkeley. He d. 1 1 May 1851, aged 41. Will pr. Jan. 1854. His widow d. 29 April 1896, at Faraday House, Hampton Court, aged 83."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524416#page/n325/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1906; Vol. V; page 303
