2 CONT (Also Vol 3 p181 - 107th edition)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1c''' Charles''', CB, JP; born 21 Sept 1821; V-Adml; married 9 Dec 1861 Augusta Judith (died 16 June 1893), daughter of William Gilbert Campion, and died 1 April 1901, leaving:
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1d John Francis; born 27 Oct 1866; Capt RN; died unmarried 10 May 1904
2 CONT * 1d Alicia Harriet; married 15 Jan 1891 Rev Alfred Evans VINTER later MURRAY-AYNSLEY (taken with arms by roy licence 15 Aug 1904; died 27 Nov 1920), Pncpl Bishop's Stortford Trg College, and died 1923, leaving issue
2 CONT
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p2266.htm#i22657
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Vice-Admiral Charles Murray-Aynsley'''1 M, #22657, b. 21 September 1821, d. 1 April 1901
2 CONT
2 CONT Vice-Admiral Charles Murray-Aynsley was born on 21 September 1821.1 He was the son of John Murray-Aynsley and Emma Sarah Peach.1 He married Augusta Judith Campion, daughter of William Gilbert Campion, on 9 December 1861.1 He died 
2 CONC on 1 April 1901 at age 79.1
2 CONT
2 CONT He held the office of Justice of the Peace (J.P.).1 He was invested as a Companion, Order of the Bath (C.B.).1 He gained the rank of Vice-Admiral in the service of the Royal Navy.1
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children of Vice-Admiral Charles Murray-Aynsley and Augusta Judith Campion'''
2 CONT * Alicia Harriet Murray-Aynsley1 d. 1923
2 CONT * Captain John Francis Murray-Aynsley1 b. 27 Oct 1866, d. 10 May 1904
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Citations'''
2 CONT
