1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Born in London, she was the illegitimate daughter of George Gordon, 5th Duke of Gordon, and Jane Graham. Her father, although he publicly acknowledged her, played little part in her life as far as can be deduced fr
2 CONC om Gordon's memoirs. In 1805–07 she spent much of her early childhood in Scotland – her first memories were playing with rocks in Newhaven. She was baptised on 6 October 1806 at St James' Church, Piccadilly, her father standing as
2 CONC  one of her godfathers.
