1 TITL Admiral Sir
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT "<strong>Sir John Gordon Sinclair, Baronet [S 1636] of Steveson and Murkley</strong>, only son and heir, born 31 July 1790 in Edinburgh; succeeded to the Baronetcy, 4 August 1795, when aged 5, entered the Royal Navy, 1800, and ser
2 CONC ved in <em>The Victory</em> under Nelson; was in command of <em>The Redwing</em> at Morjean and Cassis (1813) in the Mediterranean; Capt. 1814; Rear Admiral, 1849; Vice Admiral of the blue, 1856; Admiral, 1861; was sometime Capt. 
2 CONC of the port at Gibraltar. He married 15 June 1812, at Stonehouse, Devon, Anne, daughter of Admiral the Hon. Michael de Courcy (younger son of John, Lord Kingsale [I]), by Anne, daughter of Conway Blennerhassett. She died 23 Septem
2 CONC ber 1857, at Stevenson. He died there 12 November 1863, aged 73."
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: [http://archive.org/stream/cu31924092524382#page/n441/mode/2up Complete baronetage]; Cokayne, George E. (George Edward); 1900; Vol. II; page 422
2 CONT
2 CONT  Admiral Sir John Gordon Sinclair of Murkle, 8th Bt. was born on 31 July 1790.1 He was the son of Sir Robert Sinclair of Murkle, 7th Bt. and Lady Madelina Gordon.1 He married Anne de Courcy, daughter of Admiral Hon. Michael de Cou
2 CONC rcy and Anne Blennerhassett, on 15 June 1812.1 He died on 13 November 1863 at age 73.1
2 CONT      He succeeded as the 8th Baronet Sinclair [N.S., 1636] on 4 August 1795.1 He gained the rank of Midshipman in the Royal Navy, on H.M.S. Victory under Nelson.1 He gained the rank of Captain in 1814.1 He gained the rank of Admir
2 CONC al in 1861.1
