1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Montagu,_6th_Duke_of_Manchester
2 CONT
2 CONT George Montagu, 6th Duke of Manchester, etc. (9 July 1799 – 18 August 1855), known as Viscount Mandeville from 1799 to 1843, was a British peer and Tory Member of Parliament.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Montagu was born at Kimbolton Castle, the son of William Montagu, 5th Duke of Manchester, and was educated at Eton. He joined the Royal Navy direct from school and had been promoted to lieutenant before retiring in 1822. Fr
2 CONC om 1818 he had served on HMS Larne at Jamaica, where his father was Governor. In 1816 his father named the newly founded town of Mandeville, Jamaica after him.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Montagu was MP for Huntingdonshire 1826–1837. He succeeded his father to the dukedom in 1843.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Montagu married firstly Millicent Sparrow (25 January 1798 – Kimbolton Castle, 21 November 1848), daughter of Brig. Gen. Robert Bernard Sparrow of Brampton Park, Huntingdonshire (d. 1805), and his wife the Hon. Olivia Aches
2 CONC on (d. 12 February 1863), on 8 October 1822 at London. His father presented him with Kimbolton Castle, the family seat in Huntingdonshire and his wife brought him Brampton Park in Huntingdonshire and an estate in Ireland. He also 
2 CONC took out a lease on to Melchbourne Park, Bedfordshire.
2 CONT
2 CONT George and Millicent had four children:
2 CONT
2 CONT William Montagu, 7th Duke of Manchester (1823–1892)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Robert Montagu (1825–1902), married Ellen Cromie and Elizabeth Wade and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Frederick Montagu (5 October 1828 – 29 October 1854), who died unmarried and without issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Olivia Montagu (18 July 1830 – Greystones, Tunbridge Wells, Kent, 15 February 1922 and interred at Chillingham on 20 February 1922), married at Kimbolton Castle, Huntingdonshire, 29 January 1850 Charles Bennet, 6th Earl of Ta
2 CONC nkerville, and had issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT George Montagu married his second wife Harriet Sydney Dobbs (4 December 1834 – Ore, Sussex, 20 May/30 May 1907), daughter of Conway Richard Dobbs of Castle Dobbs, Antrim, Ireland, and wife, on 29 August 1850 at Kilroot, County Ant
2 CONC rim.
2 CONT
2 CONT George and Harriet had two children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Lady Sydney Charlotte Montagu (14 October 1851 – Keithhall, Inverurie, Aberdeen, 21 September 1932), married at St. George, Hanover Square, London, 14 August 1873 Algernon Hawkins Thomond Keith-Falconer, 9th Earl of Kintore
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord George Francis Montagu (18 January 1855 – 12 March 1882), a Lieutenant who died unmarried and without issue
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Tunbridge Wells, aged 56.
