1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Reverend Hon. Douglas Hamilton-Gordon was born on 13 March 1824. He was the son of George Hamilton-Gordon, 4th Earl of Aberdeen and Harriet Douglas. He married Lady Ellen Susan Anne Douglas, daughter of George Shol
2 CONC to Douglas, 17th Earl of Morton and Frances Theodora Rose, on 15 July 1851 at St. James's Church, Piccadilly, London, EnglandG. He died on 6 December 1901 at age 77.
2 CONT
2 CONT He graduated from Cambridge University, Cambridge, Cambridgeshire, England, with a Master of Arts (M.A.) He held the office of Chaplain-in-Ordinary to HM Queen Victoria. He held the office of Canon of Salisbury. He held the office
2 CONC  of Honorary Chaplain to HM King Edward VII.
