2 DATE 13 SEP 1883
2 ADDR
3 STAE Alabama
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On 28 Mar 1844 Stephen Reed Hood, Justice of the Peace, performed the marriage ceremony joining his sister, Mary Ann Hood, to her intended, Asa Ware, in Franklin Co., GA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Extant land ownership tax records show Stephen Reed Hood owning land in 1845 in the Captain David District, Franklin Co., GA. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Extant land ownership tax records show Stephen Reed Hood owning land in 1849 in the Captain Pool District, Jackson Co., GA.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nov 1850 US Census of Subdivision 45, Jackson Co., GA lists S.R. Hood and his family. He was a farmer with 170 acres of land valued at $500.00 cash.
2 CONT
2 CONT Records indicate that the Stephen Reed Hood family migrated from Jackson Co., GA to Cherokee Co., AL soon after Nov 1855, the birth date of Huldah J. Hood, their last GA born child. Angeline Hood, their oldest child, was 13 Y/O at
2 CONC  the time and many years later related the difficulties encountered during that adventure-filled covered wagon journey. Stephen Hood became a large landowner in Cherokee Co., AL. His occupation was farmer and he was the first Mini
2 CONC ster of the Advent Christian Church in North Alabama and, about 1857, was the founder of the Lebanon Advent Christian Church which was located in Coats Bend near the Coosa River and eight miles north of Gadsden, Alabama. See attac
2 CONC hed photo of the Lebanon Advent Church taken in early 1970s.
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1860 US Census of District 1, Cherokee Co., AL lists Stephen Reed Hood and his large family. Stephen is listed as a "Bap. Minister" with his estate valued at $3000.00.  
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Fall of 1861 shortly after the beginning of the Civil War, he helped organize a company called the "Cherokee Beauregards"  which went on to distinguish itself in many battles. The unit was named after Cherokee County and Co
2 CONC nfederate General Pierre Gustave Toutant Beauregard, the hero of Fort Sumter and the Battle of First Manassas. While Captain of Company "D" (aka Cherokee Beauregards) of the 22nd AL Infantry which was encamped at Mobile, AL during
2 CONC  that winter of 1861/2, he became severely ill and received a surgeon's certificate of disability endorsed by General Braxton Bragg, the Gulf District Commander. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He reluctantly resigned his commission on Jan. 10, 1862 and returned to Cherokee County, AL and resumed his career in the ministry, serving in that capacity until his death. His main livelihood remained farming and by 1880 he owne
2 CONC d 380 acres valued at $2325.
2 CONT
2 CONT Stephen Reed Hood is seen in the 1866 Alabama State Census of Cherokee County. He is listed in the 1870 US Census of Etowah Co., AL as a "Gospel Minister" again with his large family and is shown owning 330 acres of land valued at
2 CONC  $3000.00
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1880 US Census of Etowah Co., AL lists 62 year old Stephen Reed Hood and his 58 year old wife, Jane, and their 15 year old son, Joseph B. Hood. Stephen is listed as "minister of the gospel".  
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=33832318 Phillip Matthew Turner, Sr.] donated the land on which the Lebanon Advent Church and Cemetery were located in Coats Bend, Etowah Co., AL. The church is now disbanded 
2 CONC and the original log church, later covered with clapboard siding, was torn down in the 1970s. The pews were distributed among the parishioners. The Lebanon Cemetery was established adjoining the church with the first burial in 185
2 CONC 8 and is well maintained. I spent many "Decoration Days" at this church and adjacent cemetery as a child in the 1930s and 1940s.  See attached photo of the Lebanon Advent Church taken in early 1970s.   
2 CONT
2 CONT The children of Stephen Reed and Jane (Sewell) Hood were:
2 CONT # Angeline Hood b. 22 Oct 1842 Franklin Co., GA, d. 05 Mar 1939 Wharton Bend, Etowah Co., AL, m. Phillip Matthew Turner, Jr. 23 Dec 1873 Etowah Co., AL, bur. Lebanon Advent Cemetery, Coats Bend, Etowah Co., AL. 
2 CONT # John S. Hood b. October 1845 GA, d. 01 Jun 1862 of disease during the Civil War near Corinth, MS.   
2 CONT # Rev. William Hamilton Hood b. 11 Jan 1848 GA, d. 10 Feb 1923 Etowah Co., AL, m. 1) Charlsie A. Croft 23 Sep 1868 Gadsden, Etowah Co., AL, 2) Lougenia Manley Hudson on 31 Jan 1895 in Etowah Co., AL, 3) Myra Weaver on 15 Dec 1904 
2 CONC in Gadsden, Etowah Co., AL, bur. Lebanon Advent Cemetery, Coats Bend, Etowah Co., AL.
2 CONT # [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=61232254 James Milton Hood] b. 28 Feb 1850 Jackson Co., GA, d. 30 Dec 1914 AL, m. Mary Ellen Hale in Jan 1874 in Cherokee Co., AL, bur. Cedar Hill Methodist Cemetery, Leesbu
2 CONC rg, Cherokee Co., AL.
2 CONT # Mary Elizabeth Hood b. 26 Oct 1851 GA, d. 18 May 1882 Etowah Co., AL, m. 03 Feb 1874 James Madison Hooper, bur. Lebanon Advent Cemetery, Coats Bend, Etowah Co., AL.
2 CONT # [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=70012159 Simon Martin Hood] b. 10 Mar 1853 Franklin Co., GA, d. 02 Jan 1932 Etowah Co., AL, m. 1) Margaret "Maggie" Ethel Hale on 15 Jan 1874, 2) Laura Lee Cunningham on 10 
2 CONC Dec 1902, 3) Mary Frances Bond Kilgore on 29 May 1909, bur. Shady Grove Cemetery, Cherokee Co., AL.
2 CONT # Huldah J. Hood b. 25 Nov 1855 GA, d. 03 Nov 1891 Etowah Co., AL, m. James Alexander McCluskey on 22 Oct 1876 in Gadsden, Etowah Co., AL, bur. Lebanon Advent Cemetery, Coates Bend, Etowah Co., AL.
2 CONT # Rev. George Washington Hood b. 14 Feb 1857 Cherokee Co., AL, d. 09 Jun 1931 Athens, Howard Co., AK, occ. preacher and farmer, m. 1) Celia Catherine Hale on 31 Aug 1876 in Cherokee Co., AL, 2) Mary Elizabeth (Boothe) Keys on 25 J
2 CONC ul 1917 in Van Buren, Crawford Co., AK, 3) Alice Rowes on 03 Dec 1924 in Nashville, Howard Co., AK, 4) Clara Collins on 08 Mar 1929 in Sallisaw, Sequoyah Co., OK, bur. in White and Shelby Cemetery, Central City, Sebastian Co., AK.
2 CONC
2 CONT # Susan (Susie) A. Hood ([http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=27519815 Susan A. Hood Hale]) b. 02 Jan 1860 Cherokee Co., AL, d. 26 Aug 1903 Cherokee Co., AL, m. David Crockett Hale on 13 Oct 1879 in Etowah Co., A
2 CONC L, bur. in Lebanon Advent Cemetery, Coats Bend, Etowah Co., AL.
2 CONT # Laura Celia Hood b. 01 Dec 1861 Cherokee Co., AL, d. 02 Jun 1941 Etowah Co., AL, m. Augustus "Guss" Beauregard McCluskey on 28 Dec 1879 in Gadsden, Etowah Co., AL, bur. in Lebanon Advent Cemetery, Coats Bend, Etowah Co., AL.
2 CONT # [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=66500422 Joseph B. Hood] b. 29 Jan 1865 Cherokee Co., AL, d. 11 Oct 1933 Jenny Lind, Sebastian Co., AK, m. Unmarried, occ. coal miner, Great Western Coal Co., AK, bur. in Ol
2 CONC d Jenny Lind Cemetery, Jenny Lind, Sebastian Co, AK. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT # "The John and Richard Hood Clan of Halifax County, Virginia; Burke County, North Carolina; and Pendleton and Greenville Districts, South Carolina" by Clyde B. Hood, 2013, pp197-200.
2 CONT # Article-Estate Record of Rev. Stephen Reed Hood, Northeast Alabama Settlers, Vol. XXIX, No. 3, January 1991.
2 CONT # "The Cherokee Beauregards and the Road to Shiloh: The Military Careers of Captain Stephen R. Hood and Private John S. Hood" By George H. McCluskey, 2010.
2 CONT
