1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://archive.org/stream/scotspeeragefoun04pauluoft#page/170/mode/2up The Scots peerage], Vol. IV, page 171
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Randolph_Stewart,_9th_Earl_of_Galloway
2 CONT
2 CONT Randolph Algernon Ronald Stewart, 9th Earl of Galloway (1800–1873) was the Lord Lieutenant of Kirkcudbright from 1828 to 1845; and of Wigton from 1828 to 1851. He was styled Viscount Garlies from 1806 to 1834.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born on 16 September 1800, the eldest son of George Stewart, 8th Earl of Galloway and his wife Lady Jane Paget. He was educated at Harrow and Christ Church, Oxford and succeeded his father in 1834 to the Earldom and the fam
2 CONC ily seat of Galloway House in Dumfries and Galloway.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was MP for Cockermouth from 1826 to 1831.
2 CONT
2 CONT On 9 August 1833, he married Lady Harriet Blanche Somerset, daughter of Henry Somerset, 6th Duke of Beaufort, and had 6 sons and 7 daughters. He was succeeded in his titles and estates in turn by his eldest son Alan Stewart, 10th 
2 CONC Earl of Galloway, and his second son Randolph.
