1 NAME Frederica /Crofton/
2 GIVN Frederica
2 SURN Crofton
2 _MARNM McLaughlin
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 28 APR 1816
2 ADDR
3 CITY Mote Park
3 CTRY Ireland
1 BURI
2 DATE 28 MAY 1881
1 DEAT
2 DATE 28 MAY 1881
2 ADDR
3 STAE England
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 TITL Honorable
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Biography from http://www.harrymclaughlin.com/FredericaCrofton.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT "THE HONORABLE FREDERICA CROFTON (1816-81) was born after the suicide of her father, Sir Edward, 3rd Baronet Crofton. Frederica’s ancestry, documented in Crofton memoirs,* stemed from John Crofton who arrived in Ireland in 1565 wi
2 CONC th the Earl of Essex, and acquired land in Roscommon, Leitrim, and Sligo. From 1576 until 1597 he was Escheator General of Ireland, meaning that if property had no legal heir he seized it for Queen Elizabeth.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Crofton Baronetcy was created in 1758 for Marcus Lowther MP who took the name Crofton when he married Catherine upon whom the family estate devolved when her brother died without issue. The Barony of Crofton was created for Fr
2 CONC ederica's grandmother, Lady Anne Crofton. In 1797, just after Sir Edward Crofton, 2nd Baronet, of the Mote, had been offered a barony in the Peerage of Ireland, he died. So the honour was bestowed upon his widow instead. That enab
2 CONC led Frederica to obtain, two years after her marriage, a patent granting her the precedence of a baron's daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederica was brought up in Mote Park House, her family's home on their 7,000-acre estate at Ballymurray, Roscommon, Ireland. It was built about 1775 by John Crofton (1740-1813) to replace a castle which the Croftons erected in 16
2 CONC 20 but which had been ravaged by fire.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir Edward Crofton, 3rd Baronet Crofton, had the architect Sir Richard Morrisson design an extension for him which more than doubled the size of the house. Fire struck again in 1865: Mote Park was destroyed but was rebuilt with mo
2 CONC difications. Because of the Land Acts most of the estate was sold piecemeal early last century. The house was neglected. About 1960 the Land Commission demolished it.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederica was the youngest sister of Edward, Second Baron Crofton (left). He sat in the House of Lords as an Irish Representative Peer from 1840 to 1869 and served as a Lord-in-Waiting (government whip) in the three Conservative a
2 CONC dministrations of the Earl of Derby and in Benjamin Disraeli's first government.
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward married Lady Georgina Paget. Their daughter Augusta Caroline Crofton was the wife of Luke Dillon, Fourth Baron Clonbrock. Both were photographers, but Lady Augusta (right) was so notable that she was invested as an Officer 
2 CONC in the Order of the British Empire (OBE).
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederica's portrait on milk glass shown on a previous page was derived from the photograph at the top of this page. The lack of a name on the back of the print may indicate that it was not taken by a professional but by her niece
2 CONC  Augusta.
2 CONT
2 CONT * H. T. Crofton. Crofton memoirs : an account of John Crofton of Ballymurry, Co. Roscommon, Queen Elizabeth's escheator-general of Ireland, and of his ancestors and descendants, and others bearing the name. York. 1911. pp. 515. Do
2 CONC wnloadable through libraries subscribing to HeritageQuest Online."
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedigree from http://www.thepeerage.com/p8732.htm#i87314
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Frederica Crofton1
2 CONT
2 CONT F, #87314, b. 1816, d. 28 May 1881
2 CONT
2 CONT Hon. Frederica Crofton|b. 1816\nd. 28 May 1881|p8732.htm#i87314|Hon. Sir Edward Crofton, 3rd Bt.|b. 23 Oct 1778\nd. 8 Jan 1816|p2686.htm#i26854|Lady Charlotte Stewart|d. May 1842|p2686.htm#i26855|Sir Edward Crofton, 2nd Bt.|d. 30 
2 CONC Sep 1797|p21449.htm#i214486|Anne Croker, Baroness Crofton of Mote|b. 11 Jan 1751\nd. 12 Aug 1817|p6613.htm#i66125|John Stewart, 7th Earl of Galloway|b. 13 Mar 1736\nd. 13 Nov 1806|p10592.htm#i105918|Anne Dashwood|b. 1743\nd. 8 Jan
2 CONC  1830|p10592.htm#i105919|
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Edited=20 Dec 2008
2 CONT
2 CONT Consanguinity Index=0.0%
2 CONT
2 CONT      Hon. Frederica Crofton was born in 1816.3 She was the daughter of Hon. Sir Edward Crofton, 3rd Bt. and Lady Charlotte Stewart.2 She married Very Rev. Hubert McLaughlin, son of Thomas McLaughlin and Elizabeth Butler, on 24 Sep
2 CONC tember 1835.1 She died on 28 May 1881.1 She was buried at Boraston Church, Boraston, Shropshire, England.3
2 CONT
2 CONT      From 24 September 1835, her married name became McLaughlin. On 11 July 1837 she was granted the rank of a baron's daughter.1
2 CONT
