1 NOTE {geni:about_me} == Wikipedia Biographical Summary ==
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Rushout,_3rd_Baron_Northwick George Rushout, 3rd Baron Northwick] (30 August 1811 – 11 November 1887), was a British Conservative politician.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Background ===
2 CONT Northwick was the son of Reverend the Hon. George Rushout-Bowles, younger son of John Rushout, 1st Baron Northwick. His mother was Lady Caroline, daughter of John Stewart, 7th Earl of Galloway. He was born at Burford, Shropshire w
2 CONC here his father was then parish Rector.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was educated at Harrow School and entered Christ Church College, Oxford in 1829, graduating as BA in 1833 and MA in 1836.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Political Career ==
2 CONT Rushout was commissioned Cornet in the 1st Life Guards in 1833, was promoted Lieutenant in 1837 and Major in 1842, retiring from the army in the latter year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Northwick was in later life governor of Harrow School and Cheltenham College.
2 CONT
2 CONT === Family ===
2 CONT Lord Northwick married the Hon. Elizabeth Augusta, daughter of William Bateman-Hanbury, 1st Baron Bateman and widow of George Warburton, in 1869. There were no surviving children from the marriage, an only child, a daughter Caroli
2 CONC ne, dying aged eight in 1878. On 23 January 1886 the couple, then married sixteen years, were awarded the prize of the Dunmow Flitch, "receiving it privately and without the customary forms".
2 CONT
2 CONT Lord Northwick died at the Queen's Hotel, Upper Norwood, Surrey in November 1887, aged 76, when his titles became extinct. Lady Northwick died in May 1912, aged 80.
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: Wikipedia contributors, 'George Rushout, 3rd Baron Northwick', Wikipedia, The Free Encyclopedia, 10 January 2013, 19:18 UTC, <http://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=George_Rushout,_3rd_Baron_Northwick&oldid=532409641> 
2 CONC [accessed 18 October 2013]
