1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10153-77378/algernon-stewart-in-1871-england-wales-census MyHeritage: Algernon Stewart: 1871 England & Wales Census]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 April 1871 Census for residents of [14 Sussex Gardens, Tyburnia, London W2 1UL 51.5179811, -0.1682232], England
2 CONT * Algernon Stewart, head, widower, male, aged 60 [born about 1811], in London
2 CONT * Margaret Clement, sister-in-law, single, female, aged 56 [born about 1811], in Woolwich, Kent '''NOTE: not currently on tree'''
2 CONT * Jane Harding, servant, single, female, aged 27 [born about 1811], in Lanhydrock, Cornwall; Occupation: Cook domestic servant
2 CONT * Elizabeth Hammond, servant, single, female, aged 22 [born about 1811], in Ireland; Occupation: Housemaid domestic servant
2 CONT * Jane Thomas, servant, single, female, aged 40 [born about 1811], in Camborne, Cornwall; Occupation: Nurse domestic servant
2 CONT * 3 servants
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=W8ZRp3YpS95EqIEiWQ05xA&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of death of Algernon Stewart in 1875]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT October to December 1875: Registration of death of Algernon Stewart; aged 64 [born about 1811]; in Kensington (Volume 1a, Page 40)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10691-318968/algernon-stewart-esq-in-england-wales-index-of-wills-probates MyHeritage: Probate index 1875]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 22 November 1875 probate of Algernon Stewart, Esq. of 14 Sussex Gardens, Hyde Park, Middlesex, who died Thursday, 4 November 1875, at 14 Sussex Gardens, probate granted (will with codicil) at Principal Registry on 22 November 1875
2 CONC  to Algernon Augustus Stewart, Esq., of 14 Sussex Gardens, the son, the sole executor. Effects under £14000
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://archive.org/details/cu31924007648516/page/n65/mode/2up?q=Algernon+Stewart List of inscriptions on tombstones and monuments in Ceylon, of historical or local interest, by John Penry Lewis, Published 1913 Page 48]''
2 CONC '
2 CONT
2 CONT Sacred to the memory of Katherine Charlotte Stewart, the beloved and lamented daughter of Algernon Stewart, H. M. Ceylon Civil Service, and Charlotte Anne Clement, his wife. Born Tuesday, 3 February 1835. Died Wednesday, 30 March 
2 CONC 1836.
2 CONT
2 CONT Algernon Stewart was in the Civil Service, 1830-1850, and retired as District Judge of Galle, Monday, 18 February 1850. He married at St. Peter's, Colombo, Saturday, 23 November 1833, Charlotte Anne Clement, daughter of Lieutenant
2 CONC -Colonel Clement, R.A. (see No. 132). She died, Wednesday, 16 October 1861, at Kensington Gardens.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://archive.org/details/cu31924007648516/page/n67/mode/1up?q=%22John+Albeck+Clement%22 List of inscriptions on tombstones and monuments in Ceylon, of historical or local interest, by John Penry Lewis, Published 1913 P
2 CONC age 50]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Colonel John Albeck Clement's daughter, Charlotte Anne Clement, married, Saturday, 23 November 1833, Algernon Stewart, C.C.S. [Ceylon Civil Service]. (see No. 122).
