1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Story of descent from Bonnie Prince Charlie on mother's side: Related to him through the Stewart ancestors of the Earl's of Dunmore. Also the 3rd Earl of Dunmore had fought for Bonnie Prince Charlie.  A family story says the Marti
2 CONC n's in Scotland had a castle. The castle was Dunmore House which is near the 'Pineapple' green house. Genetic and historical evidence shows we are descended from Sir Charles Murray, second son of George Murray, 5th Earl of Dunmore
2 CONC .  
2 CONT
2 CONT The 12th Earl of Dunmore's Cousins family ancestors could be very very distantly related, however this would not then show up as genetic third cousins on gedmatch or familytreedna. That is only possible if Charles Murray was Harri
2 CONC et Jones biological father as well as all the intermarriage of his ancestors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT There are DNA matches from two American branches, one that descends from illegitimately from the 1st Marquess of Atholl and another from his father the 2nd Earl of Tullibardine. I also have a 3rd to 5th cousin match to the current
2 CONC  12th Earl of Dunmore through our common descent from the 4th Earl. We are genetically closer than on paper due to intermarriage along the Dunmore line. For example, I descend from the 1st Earl of Dunmore three times and his fathe
2 CONC r four times. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **Charles Murray states in his book meeting a western veteran who knew the six nations languages named Captain Jones in his seventies (P. 358, Travels in North America, 1839). This was Augustus Jones who was formerly a militia Cap
2 CONC tain and surveyor around Niagara Falls, Ontario, and New York.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Peter Jones named his first son Charles Augustus, which happens to be the name of D'Este's first Cousin. This proves that Peter Jones was not only close to Augustus Frederick D'Este but to Sir Charles Augustus Murray (see wikipedi
2 CONC a article) as well. He was the son of the 5th Earl of Dunmore and his grandmother was named Harriett. Charles Murray had traveled North America in 1835 after the meeting with the royal family in 1832 (Peter Jones first tour of Eng
2 CONC land). Harriett Jones is probably his illegitimate daughter when he went to North America in 1834. 
2 CONT
2 CONT A major reason why I have several distant cousin matches to this same Murray family, including a closer cousin match to the current Earl of Dunmore, is because Charles Augustus Murray's parents were first cousins meaning more of t
2 CONC he DNA was passed on down to me. D'Este probably was not the father since he had Multiple Sclerosis at the time and by his own account had reproductive problems prior to 1832. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 12th Earl of Dunmore and his brother show up as closer DNA matches than they really are probably due to the distant cousin inter-marriages in the ancestry of the 4th Earl and his wife.   We now know the truth about the story o
2 CONC f a castle in Scotland and relation to Bonnie Prince Charlie. I wouldn't have guessed it though. If Harriett Jones lived long enough it is likely more details would have survived. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Named after father's grandmother, the former Duchess of Hamilton. Her mother may have wanted to name her after a Duchess. 
2 CONT
2 CONT **Some Surname DNA matches, Murray, Douglas, Montgomerie, and Fielding/Villiers.  The Murray (Earl of Dunmore), dna matches (from familytreedna.com) are on the 17th chromosome which is where there is also a large and largest conce
2 CONC ntration of Native American dna. The previously unknown fourth great grandmother would have to be where the common ancestor is. Two DNA matches are from the 12th Earl of Dunmore and his brother who live in Australia, several from 
2 CONC a distant American branch who descend from an illegitimate son of the 2nd Earl of Tullibardine and the last known for now match is a 9th cousin match to the 6th Earl and Countess of Eglinton, ancestors of Lady Charlotte Stewart, t
2 CONC he 4th Earl of Dunmore's wife. I have another cousin match from the Earl's of Angus line which also shows up as Charlotte Stewart's ancestors. 
2 CONT
2 CONT (Douglas match: Common ancestors: A match to Archibald Douglas, 5th Earl of Angus. They descend from an illegitimate son (poss. Archibald) of James Douglas, 4th Earl of Morton, and then through his son Alexander, his son Robert b.
2 CONC  1588, and his son William b. 1610, who came to live at New London, CT. Since there are two very distant lines we both come from the genetic relationship is closer than when our common ancestors actually lived.) (Montgomerie Match
2 CONC : was from user Cheridid1 who seems to not want to talk.) (Fielding/Villiers Match: related on multiple lines)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Murray Matches:If related along Murray line, their research needs to be fixed. Their Murray line is descended from Rev. John Murray b. 1591 (later legitimized),  and Jane McClean or Elizabeth Colville; illegitimate son of William
2 CONC  Murray, 2nd Earl of Tullibardine (their 9th great grandparent). Our common ancestor is my 12th and their 9th great grandparents. 10th cousins 3x removed. Equivalent to 11-12th cousins. THERE ARE SEVERAL CONFIRMED AMERICAN COUSIN 
2 CONC MATCHES ON THE MURRAY LINE, BUT MAY HAVE DIFFERENT DESCENTS) (Second Murray Match, User: robandcarie, Both descended from the Murray line, however her line is genetically proven but the documentation is seemingly missing. Probably
2 CONC  descended from George Murray born 1658 of Henrico County, VA who was an illegitimate son of the 1st Marquess of Atholl.)
2 CONT
