1 OCCU Gentleman Landowner in Scotland & Australia. Financially independent. 
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Charles James Boehm Murray, my 2 x great grandfather, came from a wealthy family owning estates in Scotland & England. He was educated at a French boarding school with his brother Edmond John Murray for a time. The
2 CONC y were later expelled for an "unmentionable" event!!!
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles was financially independent personally owning land in Scotland & Australia.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was disliked and distrusted by Captain John Hepburn, so Charles & Alice Hepburn waited and married after Captain John Hepburn's demise.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles relinquished his parental responsibilities for the care of his daughter Eliza Marion Murray (later Mrs Murton) to Alice's brother George Stuart Hepburn to feed, clothe, house & educate. This was possibly due to the Hepburn
2 CONC  family's dislike and distrust of Charles to carry out such duties. George was executor of Captain John Hepburn's substantial estate & held responsibilities to the beneficiaries.
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles also renounced his right to administer Alice's will. This duty fell on 8 Oct 1885, to Eliza Marion Murton nee Murray of Weinteriga River Station, Darling, N.S.W, as the sole executrix, only chid & sole beneficiary of Alice
2 CONC  Elizabeth Hepburn's substantial estate. This was also possibly due to the Hepburn family's dislike and distrust of Charles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth & Baptism Records:
2 CONT 1. Ref: Boehm Family Bible dating back to 1638 (held privately by family) recorded Charles James Boehm Murray's birth date as "July 16th 1829, and Baptised August 7th 1829 at Newton House Avondale Co Lanark by Rev William Proudfoo
2 CONC t."
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. Ref: National Records of Scotland, https://www.scotlandspeople.gov.uk, 1829 MURRAY, CHARLES JAMES B (Old Parish Registers Births 621/ Avondale) Page 60 of 524.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Record:
2 CONT 1 Ref: Find a Grave Memorial ID: 250057162. 
2 CONT 2.Ref: https://www.nationaltrust.org.au/collections/hepburn-graves-smeaton-house-smeaton/ AND https://www.goldfieldsguide.com.au/explore-location/407/hepburn-graves/
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Contribution from Private Rhodes (2 x great granddaughter)
2 CONT
2 CONT NOTE: Does not appear with father John Edmund MURRAY in 1841 Census (living in France)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/250057162/charles-james_boehm-murray
2 CONT
