1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From Australian Stockman's Hall of Fame and Outback Heritage Centre
2 CONT
2 CONT Name/Title Alexander Keith COLLINS, b. 1st December 1829, British Colonies, d. 23rd April 1875, "Mitchell Downs" QLD
2 CONT
2 CONT About this object 1836: At "Ournie Station" on the Murray River with his father Captain John Gunn Collins. 1837: Attended the King's School, Parramatta, with his brother Granville, until 1843.	 1849: On the death of his father Ale
2 CONC xander established a partnership with his brother to purchase "Kimo Station" near Gundagai, New South Wales.	 1855: Married Clara Chase Stuckey, daughter of early pioneer Peter Stuckey, of "Longreach Station", Marulan, New South W
2 CONC ales. "Longreach Station" was established by Peter in 1824 and was the first "Longreach". (see MORE-INFO). Peter Stuckey is said to have crossed the Murrumbidgee River ahead of explorer Sturt.	 1857: Left "Kimo" partnership to und
2 CONC ertake various squatting and exploration expeditions in Queensland.	 Alexander was one of a party of three who were the first white men (after the explorer Kennedy) to successfully 'get through from Bourke to Rockhampton, via "Bog
2 CONC an River Station"'. He is recorded as having established the first stock route between the south and Rockhampton. He joined Charles Clarendon Cox in squatting pursuits at "Windah Station" near Rockhampton.
