1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bought Malsanger House from Sir David Thurlow Cuninghame in about 1858.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT '''Sir Wyndham Spencer Portal''', 1st Bt. was born on 22 July 1822.
2 CONT * Son of John Portal and Elizabeth Drummond. 
2 CONT * Married Mary Jane Hicks-Beach, daughter of William Hicks-Beach, on 19 April 1849.
2 CONT * Died on 14 September 1905 at age 83.3
2 CONT * Educated at Harrow School, Harrow on the Hill, London, England and at Royal Military College, Sandhurst, Berkshire, England.
2 CONT * Gained the rank of Captain between 1842 and 1865 in the service of the Hampshire Yeomanry.
2 CONT * Held the office of Justice of the Peace (J.P.) and of Deputy Lieutenant (D.L.) of Hampshire.
2 CONT * Vice-chairman and chairman of the London and South Western Railway between 1875 and 1900.3 
2 CONT * He was created 1st Baronet Portal, of Malshanger, Church Oakley, co. Southampton [U.K.] on 11 March 1901.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.thepeerage.com/p4825.htm#i48249
