1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 MAR 1835
2 ADDR
3 CITY Forres
3 STAE Scotland
3 POST IV36
3 CTRY United Kingdom
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Norman MacLeod was a British politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1828 to 1830. He was 24th Chief of the Scottish Clan MacLeod.
2 CONT
2 CONT MacLeod was born in India, the son of Major-General Norman MacLeod, later 23rd Chief of Clan MacLeod.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1828, MacLeod was elected at a by-election as a Member of Parliament (MP) for Sudbury and held the seat until 1830.
2 CONT
2 CONT MacLeod died at the age of 46 and was buried at Old Kilmuir Cemetery, Dunvegan, Skye, Scotland.
2 CONT
2 CONT MacLeod married Anne Stevenson and had nine children. His son Norman MacLeod succeeded as 25th Chief.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
