2 ADDR
3 STAE West Virginia
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/12716852
2 CONT
2 CONT Oldest of 11 children- date of birth unknown. She married a Bailey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source- Descendants of William Lake 1745-1826 by Lawrence Rex Lake
2 CONT
2 CONT http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/l/a/k/Lawrence-R-Lake/BOOK-0001/0002-0003.html
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Bond on July 8, 1815 in Harrison County, Virginia revealed an agreement between his and her parents consenting to their marriage. A fee of 150 dollars would be charged if they didn't get married.
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage Certificate revealed Enoch Bailey and Susannah Cross married on July 13, 1815 in Clarksburg, Harrison County, Virginia. John was twenty-one and Susannah was eighteen when they married. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1820 census revealed they lived in Harrison County, Virginia. Household members: Enoch Bailey (26-44), Susannah (16-25), Lewis (under 10) and Rebecca (under 10).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1830 census revealed they lived in Eastern District, Harrison County, Virginia. Household members: Enoch Bailey (30-39), Susannah (30-39), Richard (under 5), Rebecca (10-14), one female (5-9) and one female (under 5).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1840 census revealed household members: Enoch Bailey (30-39), Susannah (40-49), Peyton (under 5), one female (20-29), one female (15-19) and Edith (5-9).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1850 census revealed Enoch was a farmer and their real estate value was $500. They were all born in Virginia and lived in District 22, Harrison County, Virginia. Household members: Enoch Bailey (49), Susannah (47) and Peyton (
2 CONC 13).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1860 census revealed their real estate value was $1000, personal property value was $479 and they lived in Tyler County, Virginia. Household members: Enoch Bailey (65), Susannah (63), son, Richard (30), son, Peyton (23), Peyto
2 CONC n's wife, Nancy and daughter, Mary (1).
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1870 census revealed their real estate value was $1500, personal property value was $400. Household members: Enoch Bailey (75), Susannah (74), son, Richard (30),Richard's wife, Mary and daughter, Jane (9).
2 CONT
2 CONT Their known children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Rebecca Bailey (Elder) (b.1817 d.1902)  Lewis Bailey (b. bet.1818-1820) Richard Bailey (b.1822 d.1879) Female Bailey (b. bet.1820-1825) Female Bailey (b. bet.1826-1830) Edith Phebe Bailey (Elder)(b.1832 d.1905) Peyton Bailey (b.18
2 CONC 35 d.1882) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Enoch died one month before their fifty-fifth wedding anniversary in 1870.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah died on January 1, 1872 in Big Run, Tyler County, West Virginia.
2 CONT
2 CONT Susannah lived to age 75.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Susannah Cross Bailey BIRTH	8 May 1796 Ohio County, West Virginia, USA DEATH	1 Jan 1872 (aged 75) Tyler County, West Virginia, USA BURIAL	 Bailey Cemetery Tyler County, West Virginia,
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/12716852/susannah-bailey
2 CONT
