1 NAME Powhatan /Gordon/
2 GIVN Powhatan
2 SURN Gordon
2 _MARNM Gordon
1 NAME Maj. Powhatan Gordon
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 15 APR 1802
2 PLAC Davidson Co, TN
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE JAN 1879
2 PLAC Bryan, TX
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me}  Major Powhatan Gordon (5)(4) (10) was born on Nov 15 1802 in Nashville, Tennessee. He died on Jan 29 1879 in Bryan, Texas. Powatan Gordon was a major in the Second Seminole War, when he served in the First Tenness
2 CONC ee Mounted Militia. His life was saved when a roll-call book in his breast pocket stopped an Indian bullet. Among those under his command was the young Robert E. Lee. He had such respect for his enemy, the Seminole Chief Osceola, 
2 CONC that he named one of his sons William Osceola, which is how that Indian name entered the family. My sister's middle name, to carry on the tradition, is also Osceola.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was wounded again in the Mexican War. Tennessee troops, marching to Mexico, bivouacked on the shore of the Tennessee River at a spot they named Gordonsville in his honor. The town that developed there still bears that name. He 
2 CONC was often addressed as colonel, but the title appears to have been honorific.
2 CONT
2 CONT He farmed the land that his mother-in-law owned in Williamsport, Tennessee, on the Duck River, and lived in the fine house that she built there. He served in the Tennessee State Legislature in 1842 and again in 1845. He was quite 
2 CONC swarthy and was often known, because of his appearence and his name, as "the Indian." In one of his legislative campaigns, when he was running against Col. Terry H. Cahal, who was very fair complected, and the Rev. Barclay Martin,
2 CONC  the popular saying was that the voters could take their choice among "The white man, the preacher, and the Indian."
2 CONT
2 CONT He ran for Congress in 1856 on the "Know-Nothing" ticket but was defeated.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in Bryan, Texas, while on a visit. He was married to Caroline Mary Coleman on Jun 26 1828 in Probably Nashville, Tennessee.
2 CONT
