1 NAME Bolling /Gordon/
2 GIVN Bolling
2 SURN Gordon
2 _MARNM Gordon
1 NAME Maj. Bolling Gordon
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Rose Hill Cemetery in Columbia, Tennessee.
2 ADDR
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 APR 1800
2 PLAC Davidson Co, TN
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE NOV 1880
2 PLAC Hickman Co, TN
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Bolling Gordon was born on April 12, 1800 in Nashville, Tennessee to John and Dorothy (Crois) Gordon. He served as a surveyor in Illinois before 1830. From 1829-1835 he served in the House of Representatives of the
2 CONC  Tennessee legislature representing Hickman and Dickson counties in the 18th, 19th and 20th General Assemblies. He married Mary Elizabeth Watkins of Farmville, Virginia, daughter of Captain Joel and Mary (Jones) Watkins in 1830. I
2 CONC n 1835, he represented Hickman County, Tennessee in the State Constitutional Convention. 
2 CONT
2 CONT From 1835-1837, Gordon served in the Tennessee Senate representing Hickman, Wayne, and Lawrence counties in the 21st and 25th General Assemblies. From 1836-1840, he served as presidential elector on the Democratic ticket supportin
2 CONC g Martin Van Buren. In 1847, he was an unsuccessful candidate for Congress. In 1850, he served as a delegate to the Nashville Convention. In 1861, Gordon was elected to proposed State Convention to consider withdrawal from the Uni
2 CONC on but did not serve because of proposal to hold convention was defeated at the polls. In 1870, Gordon again represented Hickman County, Tennessee in the State Constitutional Convention. In November of 1890, Gordon died at “Cottag
2 CONC e Hill” and was buried at Rose Hill Cemetery in Columbia, Tennessee.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.tn.gov/tsla/history/manuscripts/findingaids/90-125.pdf
