1 NAME Henry Eaton /Coleman/
2 GIVN Henry Eaton
2 _MARNM Coleman
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 5 JAN 1837
1 DEAT
2 DATE 25 JUN 1890
1 OCCU
1 TITL Col. (CSA),
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/78817664/henry-eaton-coleman
2 CONT
2 CONT Born at "Woodlawn" Died at "The Oaks"
2 CONT
2 CONT 12th N.C. Inf. C.S.A.
2 CONT
2 CONT Col Henry Eaton Coleman received a serious head wound in the battle at Spotsylvania, VA. (May 12, 1864) He was taken to "Oakville" to recover from his wound. At the time, "Oakville" was the home of his wife's parents. His wife, Ju
2 CONC lia, and their two sons, Charles and Richard, were living with Julia's parents. 
2 CONT
2 CONT While still recovering from his head wound, Henry had a driver take him to the Battle of Staunton River Bridge. He was one of the heroes of this battle. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Battle_of_Staunton_River_Bridge
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia (Logan) Coleman inherited "Woodside" (home with red roof) from her parents. Henry & Julia moved in Dec 1870. They lived there until they moved back to "The Oaks", which was once the home of Julia's grandfather and uncle.
2 CONT
2 CONT Henry & Julia married Jan 27, 1858
2 CONT
2 CONT Home with green roof is "The Oaks" Cemetery is located on grounds of "The Oaks"
