1 NOTE {geni:about_me} (From: 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.victorianvilla.com/sims-mitchell/history/sims_matoaka.htm)
2 CONT
2 CONT Matoaka Whittle Sims was the daughter of James M. Whittle and his second wife (also his cousin), Cornelia Skipwith of Mecklenburg County. “Matoaka” was the Algonquian name of Chief Powhatan's daughter Pocahontas. Little Matoaka Wh
2 CONC ittle was descended from Pocahontas and John Rolfe on both sides of her family.
2 CONT
2 CONT Matoaka's mother died in 1851. James Whittle never remarried. He and his daughters (Matoaka had an older half-sister Mary, daughter of Whittle's first wife Mary Coles) continued to live at Eldon, the home he had built for Cornelia
2 CONC .In the fall of 1865 Matoaka was married to William E. Sims at her home- Eldon Plantation. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscribed initials and signatures of the Sims couple and their two boys, James and John, are still evident in the upstairs front bedroom windowpanes at Eldon.For ten years the couple shared the residence at Eldon with James Whittl
2 CONC e and his daughter Mary. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1875 James Whittle contracted for the construction of a new home (now the Sims-Mitchell House) for William and Matoaka.
