2 CONC FHL microfilm 2117658.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Greenville (Texas) Messenger, Thursday, 17 Mar 1938, page 2, J. F. BOSTICK DIED HERE LAST FRIDAY MORNING
2 CONT
2 CONT J. F. Bostick, 83, long a worthy citizen of the Tidwell community, north of Greenville, died at his home in the city last Friday morning.
2 CONT
2 CONT J. F. Bostick was a devout man of the Primitive Baptist Church and lived his religion in his home, his community and in all his dealings with his fellowman.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Alabama, coming first to Rockwall county but later moved into the Tidwell community, where he lived for many years the life of a useful citizen and a farmer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married 57 years ago to Miss Virginia Pearce, of Huntsville, Alabama, who with four children survives him.
2 CONT
2 CONT The children are: B[unreadable, probably Bernard] and Dennie Bostick and Mrs. W. E. Risener, of Tidwell and Mrs. W. E. Claiborne of Greenville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial Friday in Tidwell cemetery.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/7348671/john-floyd-bostick Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:25:36 UTC''
