2 CONC HL microfilm 2114547.
2 CONT
2 CONT Greenville (Texas) Morning Herald, Tue, 22 Nov 1955, part 1, page 6, Richard T. Bostick Of Royse City, Dies
2 CONT
2 CONT Richard T. Bostick, 95, retired farmer and a resident of Rockwall county for 70 years, died at 11:30 o'clock Sunday night at his home near Royse City.  He had been in ill health for three years.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services will be held at 2:30 o'clock this afternoon at the Munson Baptist Church near Royse City, with Rev. Andrew Bailey, of Royse City, officiating.  Burial will be in the Dry Creek community cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandsons will be pallbearers.
2 CONT
2 CONT The body will rest at the Royse City Funeral Home until the hour of the service.
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Alabama, Mr. Bostick was born on December 29, 1860 and located in Rockwall county where he had since made his home.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Mary Young in Tennessee in 1885 and she preceded him in death in 1932.
2 CONT
2 CONT Surviving are four sons, F.J. Bostick, Terrell, M.D. Bostick, California, Jess Bostick, Royse City and Bill Bostick, Terrell; two daughters, Mrs. J.T. Jones, Wichita Falls and Mrs. Dona Myers, Royse City; one brother, C.S. Bostick
2 CONC , Stephenville; 51 grandchildren, 81 great grandchildren and 11 great great grandchildren.  His wife and two daughters preceded him in death.* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21345732/richard-toliver-bostick Find A
2 CONC  Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 14 2022, 21:25:36 UTC''
