2 PLAC "Castlenau", High St
2 ADDR
3 CITY Bognor
1 OCCU Bengal Artillery
1 TITL Maj.-Gen.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Captain in Horse Artillery in India. At the time of his marriage he was a lieutenant. Major General retired (1871).
2 CONT
2 CONT From The Times, 12 April 1888
2 CONT
2 CONT The late Major-General Francis Burton Boileau, whose death occured a few days since at his residence, Castlenau, near Bognor, at the ripe age of 82, was one of the oldest members of the East India Company's forces, and long held a
2 CONC  commission in the Bengal Artillery, from which he retired on half-pay as Colonel, with the honorary rank of Major-General. He was a son of the late Mr. S. P. Boileau, and a member of the noble French Huguenot family, the Boileaus
2 CONC , Barons of Castlenau, who came to this country as refugees on the Revocation of the Edict of Nantes.
