1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=Tjpq0dlMsePbJ%2BdSoS%2FZcg&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of William Hay Gurney in 1852] and [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite
2 CONC =9skH1N0HkeYSKOPSxM3hOw&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of marriage of Anna Maria Boileau in 1852]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * July to September 1852: Registration of marriage of Anna Maria Boileau; in Henstead, Norfolk (Volume 4b, Page 317)
2 CONT * July to September 1852: Registration of marriage of William Hay Gurney; in Henstead, Norfolk (Volume 4b, Page 317)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0001945/18520911/063/0016 British Newspaper Archive: John Bull Saturday, 11 September 1852 Page 16 Married]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Wednesday, 8 September 1852 at Ketteringham, Norfolk, the Rev. William Hay Gurney, second son of Daniel Gurney, Esq., of North Runcton, and the late Lady Harriet Gurney, to Anna Maria Boileau, daughter of Sir John P. Boil
2 CONC eau, baronet, of Ketteringham, and Lady Catherine Boileau.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10152-124601609/william-h-gurney-in-1861-england-wales-census MyHeritage: William H Gurney: 1861 England & Wales Census]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 7 April 1861 Census for residents of Mance[?], Hamlet of Hardwick, Parish of North Runcton, Norfolk, England
2 CONT * William H Gurney, head, married, male, aged 33 [born about 1828], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Curate of North Runcton
2 CONT * Anna M Gurney, wife, married, female, aged 34 [born about 1827], in Tunbridge Wells, Kent
2 CONT * Montimer H Gurney, son, single, male, aged 6 [born about 1855], in North Runcton, Norfolk
2 CONT * Gerard B Gurney, son, single, male, aged 5 [born about 1856], in North Runcton, Norfolk
2 CONT * Arthur E Gurney, son, single, male, aged 3 [born about 1858], in North Runcton, Norfolk
2 CONT * Harriet E L Gurney, daughter, single, female, aged 2 [born about 1859], in North Runcton, Norfolk
2 CONT * Geoffrey K Gurney, son, single, male, aged 8 months, [born about July 1860], in North Runcton, Norfolk
2 CONT * Maria Vines, servant, widow, female, aged 29 [born about 1832], in Somerset; Occupation: Nurse domestic servant
2 CONT * Sarah Ann Nichols, servant, single, female, aged 18 [born about 1843], in Gaywood, Norfolk; Occupation: Nurse Maid domestic servant
2 CONT * Margaret C Curtis, servant, single, female, aged 21 [born about 1840], in Beeston Regis, Norfolk; Occupation: Housemaid domestic servant
2 CONT * Mary Ann Thorn [Thom?], servant, single, female, aged 20 [born about 1841], in West Winch, Norfolk; Occupation: Kitchenmaid domestic servant
2 CONT * Sarah Ann Pickrell[?], servant, single, female, aged 28 [born about 1833], in Dersingham, Norfolk; Occupation: Ladies Maid domestic servant
2 CONT * Lydia Thompson, servant, single, female, aged 46 [born about 1815], in Great Yarmouth, Norfolk; Occupation: Cook and Housekeeper
2 CONT * Edmund Buttery, servant, single, male, aged 16 [born about 1845], in Tottenhill, Norfolk; Occupation: Groom, domestic servant
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10153-7974727/william-hay-gurney-in-1871-england-wales-census MyHeritage: William Hay Gurney: 1871 England & Wales Census]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 2 April 1871 Census for residents of [https://maps.nls.uk/geo/explore/#zoom=16.4&lat=52.71886&lon=0.42992&layers=6&b=1&marker=52.718563,0.428572 North Runcton Rectory, Rectory Lane, North Runcton, Norfolk PE33 0QS 52.718563, 0.428
2 CONC 572], England
2 CONT * William Hay Gurney, head, single, male, aged 43 [born about 1828], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Rector of North Runcton
2 CONT * Anna Maria Gurney, wife, single, female, aged 44 [born about 1827], in Tunbridge Wells, Kent
2 CONT * Harriet Eva Gurney, daughter, single, female, aged 12 [born about 1859], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Scholar
2 CONT * Geoffrey Gurney, son, single, male, aged 10 [born about 1861], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Scholar
2 CONT * Winifred Gurney, daughter, single, female, aged 8 [born about 1863], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Scholar
2 CONT * Anselm Gurney, son, single, male, aged 6 [born about 1865], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Scholar
2 CONT * Kathleen Gurney, daughter, single, female, aged 5 [born about 1866], in North Runcton, Norfolk; Occupation: Scholar
2 CONT * Richenda Gurney, daughter, single, female, aged 2 [born about 1869], in North Runcton, Norfolk
2 CONT * Sarah Budding, single, female, aged 49 [born about 1822], in London; Occupation: Nurse
2 CONT * Clara Rogers[?], single, female, aged 24 [born about 1847], in [Brevy?], Leicestershire; Occupation: Serving maid
2 CONT * Dorothy Wagg, single, female, aged 25 [born about 1846], in Lynn, Norfolk; Occupation: Servant Nurse
2 CONT * Hannah Roberts, single, female, aged 17 [born about 1854], in Lynn, Norfolk; Occupation: Servant Nurse
2 CONT * Eliza Smith, single, female, aged 24 [born about 1847], in Walsingham, Norfolk; Occupation: Servant Cook
2 CONT * Elizabeth Armiger, single, female, aged 16 [born about 1855], in Sculthorpe, Norfolk; Occupation: Servant Kitchenmaid
2 CONT * Charles Lusher, single, male, aged 18 [born about 1853], in Downham, Norfolk; Occupation: Groom
2 CONT * Fanny Ducimetiere [probably Ducimetière}, single, female, aged 28 [born about 1843], in [Toiery?, possibly Thoiry], Savoie [Savoy] [France]; Occupation: governess
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.freebmd.org.uk/cgi/information.pl?cite=6Thx8L%2Bxk4hc5hkkjpDhWA&scan=1 FreeBMD: Registration of death of Annie Maria Gurney in 1897]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT October to December 1897: Registration of death of Annie Maria Gurney; aged 71 [born about 1826]; in Kings Lynn, Norfolk (Volume 4b, Page 229)
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000174/18971124/003/0001 British Newspaper Archive: Morning Post Wednesday, 24 November 1897 Page 1 Deaths]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Deaths: Gurney. — On Sunday, 21 November 1897 [inst.], at King's Lynn, Anna Maria Gurney, the wife of the Reverend William Hay Gurney, in her seventy-second year.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.britishnewspaperarchive.co.uk/viewer/bl/0000237/18971126/029/0006 British Newspaper Archive: Stamford Mercury Friday, 26 November 1897 Page 6 Local News: Lynn]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The wife of the Reverend W. H. Gurney, brother of Mr. Somerville Gurney, ex-Mayor of Lynn, and for many years Rector of North Runcton, from which position he retired six years ago, died at the [https://britishlistedbuildings.co.uk
2 CONC /101290849-the-bank-kings-lynn-and-west-norfolk-st-margarets-with-st-nicholas-ward Bank House, King's Staithe Square, King's Lynn, Norfolk PE30 1RD 52.7531051, 0.39291] on Sunday, 21 November 1897, at the age of 71. She was a daug
2 CONC hter of the late Sir John Boileau, of Kettering, first baronet, and a sister of Sir Francis Boileau. She was a constant visitor in the houses of the poor, and was ever ready to render them assistance.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/250808003/anna_maria_gurney findagrave: Anna Maria Gurney (née Boileau) (1826-1897)]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * Name: Anna Maria Gurney (née Boileau)
2 CONT * Born: 1826, Tunbridge Wells, Kent, England
2 CONT * Died: Sunday, 21 November 1897 (aged 70–71), Kings Lynn and West Norfolk, Norfolk, England
2 CONT * Buried: [All Saints Churchyard, The Green, North Runcton, Norfolk PE33 0RB 52.71554, 0.43602], England
2 CONT * About: Aged 71 buried on Wednesday, 24 November 1897 Abode Kings Lynn. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-10691-1492316/anna-maria-gurney-in-england-wales-index-of-wills-probates MyHeritage: Probate index 1897]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 December 1897 probate of Anna Maria Gurney of King's Lynn, Norfolk, (wife of the Reverend William Hay Gurney), who died Sunday, 21 November 1897, probate granted at London on 13 December 1897 to Somerville Arthur Gurney, George
2 CONC  Francis Addison Cresswell, and Cresswell Augustus Cresswell, Esquires. Effects £413 18s. 7d.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''From [https://archive.org/details/genealogicalhera01byuburk/page/702/mode/1up?view=theater&q=%22William+Hay%22 A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed gentry of Great Britain and Ireland by Sir Bernard Burke Volume 1 
2 CONC Published 1879 Page 702]'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Reverend William Hay, Rector of North Runcton; married 1852, Anna Maria Boileau, daughter of Sir John P. Boileau, baronet, by Lady Catherine Eliot, daughter of the 1st Earl of Minto, and has issue. His 3rd son, Arthur Elliot Gurne
2 CONC y, died Monday, 13 March 1865.
