1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of Thomas Proctor, a rag and bone merchant, he built up Cathay Works, Redcliff, into the headquarters of a large fertiliser manufacturing enterprise with branches in various towns in the Midlands. Created a 'mo
2 CONC del' farm estate at Wallscourt Farm, Stoke Gifford, complete with its own railway station and school. Churchwarden at St. Mary Redcliffe in 1842 and was chairman of the Restoration Committee. Personally made large donations for th
2 CONC e repair of the north porch. Also made donations to Emanuel Church, Guthrie Road, and had built and erected a fountain on the Downs. Magistrate, Alderman and Sheriff of Bristol and would have been Mayor but for his final illness. 
2 CONC He left his house, Elmdale, which he had had built, to the Corporation as the Mamsion House. 
