2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free encyclopedia
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Francis of Bourbon-Two Sicilies, Count of Trapani[1] (Full Italian name: Francesco di Paola, Principe di Borbone delle Due Sicilie[1]) (born 13 August 1827 in Naples, Two Sicilies[1]; died 24 September 1892 in Palermo, Ital
2 CONC y[1]) was a member of the House of Bourbon-Two Sicilies. Francis was the youngest child and son of Francis I of the Two Sicilies and his second wife Maria Isabella of Spain.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage and issue
2 CONT
2 CONT Francis married his niece Archduchess Maria Isabella of Austria, Princess of Tuscany, daughter of Leopold II, Grand Duke of Tuscany and his wife Princess Maria Antonia of the Two Sicilies, on 10 April 1850. Francis and Maria Isabe
2 CONC lla had five children:
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Antonietta Giuseppina Leopoldina of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (16 March 1851 - 12 September 1938)
2 CONT
2 CONT ∞ Prince Alfonso, Count of Caserta on 8 June 1868 in Rome, had 12 issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Leopoldo of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (24 September 1853 - 4 September 1870)
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Teresa Pia of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (7 January 1855 - 1 September 1856)
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Carolina of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (21 February 1856 - 7 April 1941)
2 CONT
2 CONT ∞ Andrzej Zamoyski, Count Zamoyski on 19 November 1885 in Paris, had 7 issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT Prince Ferdinando of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (25 May 1857 - 22 July 1859)
2 CONT
2 CONT Princess Maria Annunziata of Bourbon-Two Sicilies (21 September 1858 - 20 March 1873)
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Exile
2 CONT
2 CONT After the Kingdom of the Two Sicilies fell in 1861 during the Expedition of the Thousand, the royal family went into exile. First, Francis and his family went to Rome, where they were under the protection of Pope Pius IX. However,
2 CONC  the Papal States were also invaded by Victor Emmanuel II of Italy and Francis and his family fled next to France. Francis died in 1892 in Paris at 65 years of age.
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Titles, styles, honours and arms
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Titles and styles
2 CONT
2 CONT 13 August 1827 – 24 September 1892: His Royal Highness The Count of Trapani
2 CONT
2 CONT [edit]Honours
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of the Order of Saint Januarius (1830)
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of the Spanish Order of the Golden Fleece (1830)
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight of the Order of Charles III
2 CONT
2 CONT Knight Grand Cross of the Order of Saint Ferdinand and of Merit
2 CONT
