1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Marie-Joseph-Guy-Henry-Philippe de Riquet de Caraman, 18th Prince de Chimay, was a Belgian diplomat and politician. He was notable as governor of the province of Hainaut (1870-1878) and Foreign Minister (1884-1892)
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT His parents were Joseph de Riquet de Caraman, 17th Prince de Chimay, and Émilie Pellapra. His own six children included Joseph, Prince de Caraman-Chimay and Élisabeth, who married the Count of Greffulhe.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also gave private concerts, with him on violin and his wife on piano. In memory of one of these at which he had assisted, Franz Liszt dedicated a mass to Caraman-Chimay
