0 @N6000000002176689499@ NOTE The deaths of two elder brothers and his father made the young Prince Louis
1 CONT Dauphin of France in 1765 (heir to the throne), succeeding his grandfather
1 CONT Louis XV. On Louis's accession, France was impoverished and burdened with
1 CONT debts, and heavy taxation had resulted in wide spread misery among the French
1 CONT people. He was weak and incapable as a king, and not overly intelligent,
1 CONT preferring to spend time with his hobbies rather than his duties of state.
1 CONT The king was tried as a traitor and condemned to death by guillotine.
