0 @N6000000002322315602@ NOTE Field marshal, army reformer, and military theoretician who was one of the
1 CONT few allied commanders capable of defeating the French generals of the
1 CONT Napoleonic period. He modernized the Austrian army during the first decade of
1 CONT the 19th century, making it into a formidable force that contributed
1 CONT materially to Napoleon's defeat in 1813-15. Retiring in 1809, Charles took no
1 CONT further part in the Napoleonic struggles. His military writings emphasized
1 CONT the importance of strategic points, somewhat antiquated even by his own time.
