0 @N6000000002188440213@ NOTE
1 CONT
1 CONT      Louis XVII (Louis Charles), titular king of France, known in popular legend as the "lost dauphin".  The second son of King Louis XVI and Queen Marie Antoinette, he became dauphin at the death in 1789 of his elder brother. In 
1 CONC 1792 the revolutionists imprisoned him with the royal family in the Temple. After the execution in 1793 of King Louis XVI, the comte de Provence (later King Louis XVIII) proclaimed the dauphin King as Louis XVII, but he remained i
1 CONC n prison until his death. Cruel treatment by his jailer, Antoine Simon, was said to have hastened his end. His death has often been disputed; it was rumored that someone had taken the true dauphin from prison and substituted anoth
1 CONC er boy in his place. Evidence indicates that the boy really died in prison in 1795, and historians, for the most part, disregard the lost dauphin theory altogether.
0 @N6000000002240844113@ NOTE The son and Dauphin (heir) of Louis XVI, 8-year old Louis was recognized as
