0 @N6000000002176686797@ NOTE Became pretender to Spanish throne when brother aborted (1830) the Salic Law
1 CONT favoring male heirs, securing throne for daughter, Isabelle II. Carlos was
1 CONT recognized as King Charles V by supporters and revolted in Carlist wars
1 CONT 1833-39 but was overcome by government forces. Fleeing to France in 1839, he
1 CONT resigned pretensions in favor of his son, Don Carlos 2nd in 1845.
