0 @N6000000004867657063@ NOTE Charles Gordon-Lennox, 5th Duke of Richmond and Lennox (3 A ugust 1791 - 21 October 1860) was an English politician an d a prominent Conservative. The son of Charles Lennox, 4t h Duke of Richmond and Lady Charlotte Gordon, he was 
1 CONC style d Earl of March until he succeeded his father in 1819.
1 CONT
1 CONT He served on Wellington's staff in the Peninsular War, bein g at the same time Member of Parliament for Chichester. H e was afterwards a vehement opponent in the House of Lord s of Roman Catholic emancipation (See Gordon Riots), a
1 CONC nd a t a later date a leader of the opposition to Peel's free tr ade policy. In 1836, on inheriting the estates of his mater nal uncle, the fifth and last Duke of Gordon, he assumed th e name of Gordon before that of Lennox.
1 CONT
1 CONT [edit] Family
1 CONT
1 CONT He married Lady Caroline Paget (daughter of the Marquess o f Anglesey by Caroline Villiers) on April 10, 1817. The cou ple had eight children:
1 CONT
1 CONT     * Charles Gordon-Lennox, 6th Duke of Richmond (1818-190 3)
1 CONT     * Lady Caroline Amelia Gordon-Lennox (18 June 1819 - 3 0 April 1890), married John Ponsonby, 5th Earl of Bessborou gh
1 CONT     * Fitzroy George Charles Gordon-Lennox (11 June 182 0 - 1841), lost at sea aboard SS President
1 CONT     * Rt. Hon. Lord Henry Charles George Gordon-Lennox (2 N ovember 1821 - 29 August 1886), married Amelia Brooman an d left no issue
1 CONT     * Captain Lord Alexander Francis Charles Gordon-Lenno x (14 June 1825 - 22 January 1892), married Emily Townele y and left issue
1 CONT     * Lady Augusta Catherine Gordon-Lennox (January 14, 182 7 - 3 April 1904), married Prince Edward of Saxe-Weimar (18 23-1902)
1 CONT     * Lord George Charles Gordon-Lennox (22 October 182 9 - 27 February 1877), married Minnie Palmer and left no is sue
1 CONT     * Lady Cecilia Catherine Gordon-Lennox (April 13, 183 8 - October 5, 1910), married Charles Bingham, 4th Earl o f Lucan
